(400557, 15, 5, 'Spawn of Galakras', 400557, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400557, 6, 1, 'This formidable creature\'s lineage may be traced to Galakras, and yet further to Galakrond, one of the most infamous of all proto-dragons.', -1, 0),
(400558, 15, 5, 'Kor\'kron War Wolf', 400558, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400558, 6, 1, 'The Kor\'kron use only the mightiest wolves for their mounts, bedecking them in armor that would break the backs of lesser creatures.', -1, 0),
(400559, 15, 5, 'Kor\'kron Juggernaut', 400559, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400559, 6, 1, 'The Kor\'kron Juggernaut is a weapon of unbridled destruction, born from the mind of Garrosh Hellscream and made real by his engineers.', -1, 0),
(400560, 15, 5, 'Ashhide Mushan Beast', 400560, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400560, 6, 1, 'Some people say that riding an ashhide mushan will result in favorable health and increased prosperity. These people are called "mount vendors."', -1, 0),
(400561, 15, 5, 'Thundering Onyx Cloud Serpent', 400561, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400561, 6, 1, 'This ebony cloud serpent is a lightning-wreathed vision of such rarity as to have driven many mortals to madness.', -1, 0),
(400562, 15, 5, 'Tyrannical Gladiator\'s Cloud Serpent', 400562, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400562, 6, 1, 'These cloud serpents always look elegant and slim in classic black.', -1, 0),
(400563, 15, 5, 'Grievous Gladiator\'s Cloud Serpent', 400563, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400563, 6, 1, 'These brilliantly colored cloud serpents have scales that are a mixture of ruby, gold, and nearly violet.', -1, 0),
(400564, 15, 5, 'Prideful Gladiator\'s Cloud Serpent', 400564, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400564, 6, 1, 'These brilliantly colored cloud serpents have scales that range from gold to pink. Or we could call it coral.', -1, 0),
(400568, 15, 5, 'Emerald Hippogryph', 400568, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400568, 6, 1, 'These majestic animals come in various colorings, but the emerald variety can only be tamed by the magic of friendship.', -1, 0),
(400571, 15, 5, 'Iron Skyreaver', 400571, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400571, 6, 1, 'Iron Horde beastmasters bred this rylak for war and then girded it for battle in black steel and smoldering flame.', -1, 0),
(400593, 15, 5, 'Warforged Nightmare', 400593, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400593, 6, 1, 'A nightmarish steed of hardened steel and vengeful spirits, this companion will follow you to the depths of the Firelands and back without complaint.', -1, 0),
(400594, 15, 5, 'Grinning Reaver', 400594, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400594, 6, 1, 'The difference between a smile and a grin is the difference between a kiss and tasting.', -1, 0),
(400600, 15, 5, 'Dread Raven', 400600, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400600, 6, 1, 'Filled with the hatred of an ancient god, the dread raven are the Arakkoa\'s most trusted guardians.', -1, 0),
(400603, 15, 5, 'Creeping Carpet', 400603, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400603, 6, 1, 'Can\'t fly, but can creep very quickly.', -1, 0),
(400606, 15, 5, 'Core Hound', 400606, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400606, 6, 1, 'Molten to the core!', -1, 0),
(400607, 15, 5, 'Gorestrider Gronnling', 400607, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400607, 6, 1, 'Once "befriended", a gronnling will happily carry its rider to their death.', -1, 0),
(400608, 15, 5, 'Witherhide Cliffstomper', 400608, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400608, 6, 1, 'Tiny notches cover the hooves of this variation of clefthoof, allowing it to safely scale mountainous regions in search of food.', -1, 0),
(400609, 15, 5, 'Trained Icehoof', 400609, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400609, 6, 1, 'It wasn\'t until you owned this mount that you understood how much the world of Draenor would test you. Clefthoof hair gets in everything!', -1, 0),
(400611, 15, 5, 'Tundra Icehoof', 400611, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400611, 6, 1, 'A translucent layer of down hair covers this breed\'s leathery hide, acting as the perfect insulation for cold environments.', -1, 0),
(400612, 15, 5, 'Bloodhoof Bull', 400612, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400612, 6, 1, 'Members of the Warsong clan have long hunted these clefthoof to use their crimson-hued skin for battle standards.', -1, 0),
(400613, 15, 5, 'Ironhoof Destroyer', 400613, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400613, 6, 1, 'Blackhand is said to have personally designed the fiery armaments used on the Iron Horde\'s clefthoof battle mounts.', -1, 0),
(400614, 15, 5, 'Mottled Meadowstomper', 400614, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400614, 6, 1, 'The elekk\'s long trunk allows it to sniff out sources of food, avoid danger, and steal snacks from your bags when you\'re not looking.', -1, 0),
(400615, 15, 5, 'Trained Meadowstomper', 400615, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400615, 6, 1, 'The draenei perfected elekk husbandry long ago, adorning the creatures with Light-infused crystals to make them more docile.', -1, 0),
(400616, 15, 5, 'Shadowhide Pearltusk', 400616, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400616, 6, 1, 'Some legends say the draenei first befriended the elekk after one of the beasts saved an injured scout from a pack of vicious podlings.', -1, 0),
(400617, 15, 5, 'Dusty Rockhide', 400617, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400617, 6, 1, 'Ever since acquiring this mount, you have been plagued by strange fever dreams of hippety-hoppety clippety-cloppety elekk on parade.', -1, 0),
(400618, 15, 5, 'Armored Irontusk', 400618, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400618, 6, 1, 'It is said an elekk never forgets. No wonder it despises the Iron Horde, considering the torment the orcs put the beast through.', -1, 0),
(400619, 15, 5, 'Blacksteel Battleboar', 400619, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400619, 6, 1, 'Refuses to run unless its head is covered in heavy, spiked metal. It\'s an ego thing.', -1, 0),
(400620, 15, 5, 'Rocktusk Battleboar', 400620, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400620, 6, 1, 'It\'s not the metal helmet that attracts mates; it\'s the sweet mohawk.', -1, 0),
(400621, 15, 5, 'Armored Frostboar', 400621, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400621, 6, 1, 'Subsists almost entirely on a diet of frozen berries. Though it finds slow off-worlders equally tasty.', -1, 0),
(400622, 15, 5, 'Armored Razorback', 400622, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400622, 6, 1, 'Never... ever... EVER... let it smell bacon on you.', -1, 0),
(400623, 15, 5, 'Frostplains Battleboar', 400623, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400623, 6, 1, 'If it didn\'t have the cool tusk ring, it would feel so silly in that outfit.', -1, 0),
(400624, 15, 5, 'Wild Goretusk', 400624, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400624, 6, 1, 'If you want a gentle ride, go find a "tame happytusk" or something.', -1, 0),
(400625, 15, 5, 'Domesticated Razorback', 400625, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400625, 6, 1, 'Domesticated does not mean "friendly." Bring some treats.', -1, 0),
(400626, 15, 5, 'Giant Coldsnout', 400626, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400626, 6, 1, 'Its snout is not just cold but wet. Not a pleasant way to wake up.', -1, 0),
(400627, 15, 5, 'Great Greytusk', 400627, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400627, 6, 1, 'Sheds its tusks once a year. Is extremely shy until they grow back.', -1, 0),
(400628, 15, 5, 'Trained Rocktusk', 400628, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400628, 6, 1, 'Thoroughly trained in how to snort, trot, and stomp on the faces of its enemies.', -1, 0),
(400629, 15, 5, 'Trained Riverwallow', 400629, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400629, 6, 1, 'Riverwallows are one of the heartiest beasts on Draenor, resulting in their increased stamina and distinctive coloring.', -1, 0),
(400630, 15, 5, 'Sapphire Riverbeast', 400630, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400630, 6, 1, 'This animal\'s color mimics the clear blue of Draenor\'s river shallows, making it almost invisible to aquatic predators.', -1, 0),
(400631, 15, 5, 'Mudback Riverbeast', 400631, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400631, 6, 1, 'Special webbing that grows on the soles of the mudback\'s feet gives them extra traction in mud and slick terrain.', -1, 0),
(400632, 15, 5, 'Mosshide Riverwallow', 400632, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400632, 6, 1, 'Aggressive and territorial, the mosshide is known for hiding in river-shore scrub and ambushing unwary passersby.', -1, 0),
(400633, 15, 5, 'Hellfire Infernal', 400633, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400633, 6, 1, 'From the bowels of the nether is summoned a creature of pure hatred, bent on burning down any life in its way.', -1, 0),
(400634, 15, 5, 'Solar Spirehawk', 400634, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400634, 6, 1, 'Looking into the eyes of this mystical beast is like peering into the heart of the sun. Goggles are recommended when you\'re riding.', -1, 0),
(400635, 15, 5, 'Shadowmane Charger', 400635, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400635, 6, 1, 'Draenei poets have likened this talbuk\'s coloring to shadows cast by moonlight in an ashen forest.', -1, 0),
(400636, 15, 5, 'Swift Breezestrider', 400636, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400636, 6, 1, 'Draenei have relied on this mount, the swiftest of all talbuk, to relay messengers and their missives safely to their destinations.', -1, 0),
(400637, 15, 5, 'Trained Silverpelt', 400637, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400637, 6, 1, 'Prized for its intelligence, this breed of talbuk can be trained to execute defensive kicks and gorings in battle.', -1, 0),
(400638, 15, 5, 'Breezestrider Stallion', 400638, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400638, 6, 1, 'These breezestriders\' red coloration reflects their temperament: sanguine, fierce, and courageous.', -1, 0),
(400639, 15, 5, 'Pale Thorngrazer', 400639, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400639, 6, 1, 'This talbuk subsists completely on a diet of thistles and thorns, making its insides as tough as its outside.', -1, 0),
(400640, 15, 5, 'Vicious War Ram', 400640, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400640, 6, 1, 'Until it head-butts you below the belt, it has not truly accepted you as its rider.', -1, 0),
(400641, 15, 5, 'Vicious War Raptor', 400641, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400641, 6, 1, 'Because sharp teeth and claws weren\'t enough.', -1, 0),
(400642, 15, 5, 'Garn Steelmaw', 400642, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400642, 6, 1, 'A trainer once tried to put decorative metal in his steelmaw wolf\'s mouth. He had to wait three days to get it back.', -1, 0),
(400643, 15, 5, 'Warsong Direfang', 400643, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400643, 6, 1, 'Has a will of iron but is a sweetheart if you give it a clefthoof bone to chew on.', -1, 0),
(400644, 15, 5, 'Armored Frostwolf', 400644, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400644, 6, 1, 'It\'s trained to survive the harsh climate of Frostfire Ridge, so it snuggles as if its life depended on it.', -1, 0),
(400645, 15, 5, 'Ironside Warwolf', 400645, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400645, 6, 1, 'It has an armored spike on its tail. Scratch its belly at your own risk.', -1, 0),
(400646, 15, 5, 'Coldflame Infernal', 400646, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400646, 6, 1, 'The strange icy flames cause you to sweat and shiver at the same time.', -1, 0),
(400647, 15, 5, 'Trained Snarler', 400647, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400647, 6, 1, 'Enormously cute as a puppy. Slightly less so now.', -1, 0),
(400648, 15, 5, 'Swift Frostwolf', 400648, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400648, 6, 1, 'Amidst the cold heights of Frostfire, the frostwolves hunt anything they can catch. The fastest among them eat well.', -1, 0),
(400649, 15, 5, 'Smoky Direwolf', 400649, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400649, 6, 1, 'Believed to reside mostly in the north. Hates weddings.', -1, 0),
(400650, 15, 5, 'Dustmane Direwolf', 400650, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400650, 6, 1, 'Cautious by direwolf standards, the dustmane can only be coaxed to ride with something it considers special.', -1, 0),
(400651, 15, 5, 'Warlord\'s Deathwheel', 400651, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400651, 6, 1, 'Often referred to as the "Goblin Lawn Mower", this growling behemoth treats enemies like they are made of grass... ready to be mown down.', -1, 0),
(400652, 15, 5, 'Champion\'s Treadblade', 400652, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400652, 6, 1, 'Forged by human, gnome, and dwarf, this armored masterpiece is designed to slice a tauren into a tri-tip dinner with a flick of the handlebars.', -1, 0),
(400654, 15, 5, 'Challenger\'s War Yeti', 400654, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400654, 6, 1, 'Thankfully they move fast and mostly leave the smell behind them.', -1, 0),
(400655, 15, 5, 'Sunhide Gronnling', 400655, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400655, 6, 1, 'Loves the sun, hates everything else.', -1, 0),
(400656, 15, 5, 'Llothien Prowler', 400656, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400656, 6, 1, 'These sleek foxes can prowl amongst newly-fallen leaves without making a sound, even at this size.', -1, 0),
(400657, 15, 5, 'Garn Nighthowl', 400657, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400657, 6, 1, 'The garn are the most fierce predators on Draenor, and always hunt in packs.', -1, 0),
(400663, 15, 5, 'Bloodfang Widow', 400663, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400663, 6, 1, 'Its long, serrated limbs drip with the blood of its enemies and/or mate.', -1, 0),
(400664, 15, 5, 'Emerald Drake', 400664, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400664, 6, 1, 'Is the emerald drake rare? You have no idea. If I had a silver for every time someone asked me about one, I could have retired years ago. -Mei Francis', -1, 0),
(400678, 15, 5, 'Chauffeured Mechano-Hog', 400678, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400678, 6, 1, 'Why drive yourself around when you can hire someone to do it for you?', -1, 0),
(400679, 15, 5, 'Chauffeured Mekgineer\'s Chopper', 400679, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400679, 6, 1, 'Transportation is a precise business.', -1, 0),
(400682, 15, 5, 'Voidtalon of the Dark Star', 400682, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400682, 6, 1, 'Corrupted by the presence of the Dark Star in Draenor, the Voidtalons resisted being broken by the Shadowmoon Clan and were ultimately destroyed by Ner\'zhul. Only a single egg remains, lost in the void.', -1, 0),
(400741, 15, 5, 'Mystic Runesaber', 400741, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 400741, 6, 1, 'Infused with arcane power, the Mystic Runesaber has long been hidden by chaotic nether energies. Recently they have emerged from the shadows in search of ley lines to sate their thirst for magic.', -1, 0),
