(401206, 15, 5, 'Blue Marsh Hopper', 401206, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401206, 6, 1, 'That squishing sound every time it takes a step? That\'s a feature.', -1, 0),
(401207, 15, 5, 'Yellow Marsh Hopper', 401207, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401207, 6, 1, 'No one makes giant, slimy spawns like Krag\'wa the Huge.', -1, 0),
(401208, 15, 5, 'Saltwater Seahorse', 401208, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401208, 6, 1, 'These giant seahorses are naturally curious, and are often found exploring sunken ship wreckage for shiny things.', -1, 0),
(401209, 15, 5, 'Stonehide Elderhorn', 401209, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401209, 6, 1, 'Stonehide elderhorns, one of the few types of moose to inhabit island climates, have thinner fur than most elderhorns.', -1, 0),
(401210, 15, 5, 'Bloodthirsty Dreadwing', 401210, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401210, 6, 1, 'The forsaken prefer the use of these bloodthirsty hunters, both for their speed as a mount, and the psychological effect they have on their enemies.', -1, 0),
(401211, 15, 5, 'Bloodgorged Hunter', 401211, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401211, 6, 1, 'If he wasn\'t so full, you wouldn\'t have caught him.', -1, 0),
(401212, 15, 5, 'Island Thunderscale', 401212, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401212, 6, 1, 'One of the larger native dragon species on Azeroth, this subspecies subsists almost entirely on fish. And fishermen.', -1, 0),
(401213, 15, 5, 'Risen Mare', 401213, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401213, 6, 1, 'Something terrible happened in the lost town of Havenswood.', -1, 0),
(401214, 15, 5, 'Azureshell Krolusk', 401214, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401214, 6, 1, 'Captured from the desolate sands of Vol\'dun, this mount is surprisingly docile in captivity.', -1, 0),
(401215, 15, 5, 'Rubyshell Krolusk', 401215, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401215, 6, 1, 'Captured from the desolate sands of Vol\'dun, this mount is surprisingly docile in captivity.', -1, 0),
(401216, 15, 5, 'Priestess\' Moonsaber', 401216, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401216, 6, 1, 'Once these elegant cats were only given to high-ranking priestesses of Elune, but now they ride into battle with all manner of champion, in the service of vengeance.', -1, 0),
(401218, 15, 5, 'Dazar\'alor Windreaver', 401218, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401218, 6, 1, 'Soaring high above the Battle of Dazar\'alor, these beasts are drawn to the most cunning of victors.', -1, 0),
(401219, 15, 5, 'Glacial Tidestorm', 401219, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401219, 6, 1, 'Though she commands a variety of magical powers, Jaina has always been most proficient at summoning powerful elementals of water and ice.', -1, 0),
(401220, 15, 5, 'Bruce', 401220, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401220, 6, 1, 'BRUCE!', -1, 0),
(401221, 15, 5, 'Hogrus, Swine of Good Fortune', 401221, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401221, 6, 1, 'Hogrus was first seen by Emperor Shaohao on the third day of his meditation, and is considered by the Pandaren to be a sign of good fortune to come to those who take action.', -1, 0),
(401222, 15, 5, 'Vulpine Familiar', 401222, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401222, 6, 1, 'A fiercely intelligent and curious species, these fox-like creatures have travelled the Great Dark Beyond and found their way to Azeroth. Drawn to Azeroth\'s champions, they seek adventure and companionship.', -1, 0),
(401223, 15, 5, 'Sylverian Dreamer', 401223, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401223, 6, 1, 'An artist in the magical city of Dalaran fell asleep on her brush, and dreamed of painting a beautiful feathered dragon. Her artwork leapt from the page, and when she awoke, she found it sleeping gently beside her.', -1, 0),
(401224, 15, 5, 'Wonderwing 2.0', 401224, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401224, 6, 1, 'Don\'t ask what happened to the first one -- Mechagon technology is still gnome technology!', -1, 0),
(401225, 15, 5, 'Crusader\'s Direhorn', 401225, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401225, 6, 1, 'A loyal steed to the holy crusaders of Zandalar.', -1, 0),
(401227, 15, 5, 'Aerial Unit R-21/X', 401227, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401227, 6, 1, 'King Mechagon\'s private aerial unit, complete with deployable blast cannon and foot warmers.', -1, 0),
(401229, 15, 5, 'Rusty Mechanocrawler', 401229, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401229, 6, 1, 'The check engine light is always on, it\'s when it goes off that you should be worried.', -1, 0),
(401230, 15, 5, 'Unshackled Waveray', 401230, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401230, 6, 1, 'The Unshackled have a natural kinship with the species of the deep seas that have seen cruelty at the hands of the naga.', -1, 0),
(401231, 15, 5, 'Ankoan Waveray', 401231, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401231, 6, 1, 'The Ankoan have been battling the naga for years, and with a natural affinity for the sea, training the local wildlife was a natural strategy.', -1, 0),
(401232, 15, 5, 'Azshari Bloatray', 401232, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401232, 6, 1, 'The naga raised these rays in captivity, harvesting their gas organs to craft alchemy which allowed them to breathe air more easily.', -1, 0),
(401237, 15, 5, 'Royal Snapdragon', 401237, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401237, 6, 1, 'Captured at a young age and raised to serve naga hunters, snapdragons are loyal and fierce companions.', -1, 0),
(401238, 15, 5, 'Snapback Scuttler', 401238, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401238, 6, 1, 'Giant crabs are native to Nazjatar and a favored food of the naga. This one must have been well-kept to grow this large.', -1, 0),
(401239, 15, 5, 'X-995 Mechanocat', 401239, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401239, 6, 1, 'The X-995 is the ultimate in customizeable feline robo-companionship.', -1, 0),
(401240, 15, 5, 'Obsidian Worldbreaker', 401240, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401240, 6, 1, 'I have had many names throughout history, all of them spoken with dread: Neltharion, Xaxas, and many more. Yet you shall know me best as Deathwing, for so I am!', -1, 0),
(401242, 15, 5, 'Beastlord\'s Irontusk', 401242, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401242, 6, 1, 'One of Darmac\'s trained beasts, its tusks can pierce even the hardest Iron Horde steel.', -1, 0),
(401243, 15, 5, 'Beastlord\'s Warwolf', 401243, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401243, 6, 1, 'One of Darmac\'s trained beasts, it was raised in a crucible of molten fire and shows no fear.', -1, 0),
(401245, 15, 5, 'Bloodflank Charger', 401245, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401245, 6, 1, 'Stolen from the Arathi Basin stables, this fire-hearted charger now steeds for the Horde.', -1, 0),
(401246, 15, 5, 'Ironclad Frostclaw', 401246, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401246, 6, 1, 'Captured in the snows of Alterac Valley, this bloodthirsty hunter now roars for the Alliance.', -1, 0),
(401247, 15, 5, 'Mechacycle Model W', 401247, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401247, 6, 1, 'The rapid technological evolution of the descendants of Mimiron began with the introduction of a new gear, leading to such wonders as the tragically under-produced Model W.', -1, 0),
(401248, 15, 5, 'Junkheap Drifter', 401248, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401248, 6, 1, 'When you really want to be noticed... and don\'t mind strapping yourself to a giant, barely-held-together wheel.', -1, 0),
(401249, 15, 5, 'Child of Torcali', 401249, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401249, 6, 1, 'This daughter of the great direhorn loa, Torcali, never lost faith that her keeper would help her grow to her full potential.', -1, 0),
(401250, 15, 5, 'Mollie', 401250, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401250, 6, 1, 'The kind nature of alpacas makes them perfect as companions for the intrepid adventurer.', -1, 0),
(401252, 15, 5, 'Mechagon Peacekeeper', 401252, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401252, 6, 1, 'Keeps the peace by turning you into pieces.', -1, 0),
(401253, 15, 5, 'Scrapforged Mechaspider', 401253, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401253, 6, 1, 'You built this yourself, you should be proud, even though it\'s smoky, sparky, and loud.', -1, 0),
(401254, 15, 5, 'Rustbolt Resistor', 401254, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401254, 6, 1, 'R E S I S T is carved into the seat in crude letters, along with several, more profane things.', -1, 0),
(401255, 15, 5, 'Deepcoral Snapdragon', 401255, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401255, 6, 1, 'The snapdragon is a quiet hunter in the water, but is far less stealthy on land.', -1, 0),
(401256, 15, 5, 'Snapdragon Kelpstalker', 401256, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401256, 6, 1, 'When a snapdragon bites you, the worry isn\'t about the bite itself, but the poison that will begin to eat away at the wound.', -1, 0),
(401257, 15, 5, 'Silent Glider', 401257, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401257, 6, 1, 'Gasses naturally stored within the creature allowed it to survive within the depths, those same gasses also allow them to effortlessly float through the air.', -1, 0),
(401258, 15, 5, 'Fabious', 401258, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401258, 6, 1, 'He emerges from the water, fins swaying lazily in the breeze, sun-kissed scales glittering. He is... Fabious.', -1, 0),
(401259, 15, 5, 'Silver Tidestallion', 401259, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401259, 6, 1, 'This tidestallion and its silvery scales were drawn to the glint of plunder in your pocket.', -1, 0),
(401260, 15, 5, 'Crimson Tidestallion', 401260, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401260, 6, 1, 'The blood-red coloration of these creatures is ideal for hiding in large coral formations.', -1, 0),
(401262, 15, 5, 'Inkscale Deepseeker', 401262, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401262, 6, 1, 'Schools of tidestallions will viciously slam their muscular chests into their prey to take them down.', -1, 0),
(401265, 15, 5, 'Uncorrupted Voidwing', 401265, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401265, 6, 1, 'This spawn of Vexiona, cleansed by Wrathion, comes from a flight with a fractured past and uncertain future.', -1, 0),
(401266, 15, 5, 'Alabaster Stormtalon', 401266, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401266, 6, 1, 'Chiseled by the stonemasons of Stormwind, this stone gryphon symbolizes the unbending courage of the Alliance.', -1, 0),
(401267, 15, 5, 'Alabaster Thunderwing', 401267, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401267, 6, 1, 'Chiseled by the stoneworkers of Orgrimmar, this stone wind rider is a symbol of the unwavering strength of the Horde.', -1, 0),
(401269, 15, 5, 'Swift Spectral Fathom Ray', 401269, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401269, 6, 1, 'Even the dead need a lift every now and then.', -1, 0),
(401277, 15, 5, 'Honeyback Hivemother', 401277, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401277, 6, 1, 'Destined to become queen of her hive, she scouts Kul Tiras and Zandalar in search of a suitable home for a new colony to flourish.', -1, 0),
(401282, 15, 5, 'Black Serpent of N\'Zoth', 401282, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401282, 6, 1, 'The black serpents of N\'Zoth are the harbingers of his ultimate vision becoming reality. Only those servants or enemies that can tread this space have any chance of wrangling them.', -1, 0),
(401283, 15, 5, 'Mechagon Mechanostrider', 401283, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401283, 6, 1, 'The best mount, logically, serves multiple purposes -- sometimes you need to get places AND reach something high up once you get there.', -1, 0),
(401285, 15, 5, 'Frostwolf Snarler', 401285, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401285, 6, 1, 'Raised in the Alterac Mountains by the Frostwolf Clan, trained to bite dwarves.', -1, 0),
(401286, 15, 5, 'Caravan Hyena', 401286, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401286, 6, 1, 'The canopy atop this dune-wanderer can be stored at your campsite, should you desire to feel the wind in your fur.', -1, 0),
(401287, 15, 5, 'Explorer\'s Jungle Hopper', 401287, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401287, 6, 1, 'For when you\'re making a crash landing in the middle of an uncharted swamp because it\'s the only way to access that ancient temple.', -1, 0);
INSERT INTO `item_template` (`entry`, `class`, `subclass`, `name`, `displayid`, `Quality`, `Flags`, `BuyPrice`, `SellPrice`, `ItemLevel`, `RequiredSkill`, `RequiredSkillRank`, `delay`, `spellid_1`, `spellcharges_1`, `spellid_2`, `spelltrigger_2`, `bonding`, `description`, `Material`, `BagFamily`) VALUES
(401288, 15, 5, 'Explorer\'s Dunetrekker', 401288, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401288, 6, 1, 'The surly dunetrekker can easily carry a set of explorers to the nearest ruins and back without the need to rest.', -1, 0),
(401289, 15, 5, 'Ensorcelled Everwyrm', 401289, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401289, 6, 1, 'Anima is a fundamental force that infuses the Shadowlands. It flows through many creatures, but is also traded, bartered for, and fought over.', -1, 0),
(401290, 15, 5, 'Squeakers, the Trickster', 401290, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401290, 6, 1, 'The locals in Halfhill swear that whenever a batch of grain is missing, a farmworking instrument is misplaced, or a bushel of berries can\'t be found, you can hear a mischievous squeaking, and are reminded to slow down and accept what life gives you.', -1, 0),
(401291, 15, 5, 'Lucky Yun', 401291, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401291, 6, 1, 'The Pandaren believe that merely rubbing one\'s hands on the shiny hide of the ox will grant prosperity, the challenge is catching it.', -1, 0),
(401292, 15, 5, 'Stormpike Battle Ram', 401292, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401292, 6, 1, 'Raised in the Alterac Mountains by the Stormpike Clan, trained to headbutt orcs.', -1, 0),
(401293, 15, 5, 'Ny\'alotha Allseer', 401293, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401293, 6, 1, 'To find him, drown yourself in the Circle of Stars.', -1, 0),
(401297, 15, 5, 'Clutch of Ha-Li', 401297, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401297, 6, 1, 'The brood of Ha-Li are comfortable in the blue skies of Pandaria, hunting unsuspecting prey.', -1, 0),
(401298, 15, 5, 'Hopecrusher Gargon', 401298, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401298, 6, 1, 'Once the loyal mount of a House Briarbane lord, it turned on the lord and his retinue. Members of House Briarbane now whisper of a dark Gargon lying in wait even baiting venthyr who venture through the darker parts of the Chalice District of Revendreth.', -1, 0),
(401299, 15, 5, 'Battle Gargon Vrednic', 401299, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401299, 6, 1, 'Prince Renathal\'s loyal gargon, Vrednic has been by his side for millennia. Adorned in his Sinvyr armor, Vrednic\'s mere presence instills terror to all those who lay eyes on him as he ushers his rider into battle.', -1, 0),
(401302, 15, 5, 'Dreamlight Runestag', 401302, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401302, 6, 1, 'Runestags are granted to those who have pledged their service to the Winter Queen and the Court of Night.', -1, 0),
(401303, 15, 5, 'Enchanted Dreamlight Runestag', 401303, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401303, 6, 1, 'The majestic runestags are capable of siphoning anima from the ambient light of Ardenweald with their elaborate antlers. The anima is used as nourishment and to power the runestag\'s speed and magic.', -1, 0),
(401304, 15, 5, 'Mawsworn Soulhunter', 401304, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401304, 6, 1, 'Soulhunters are used to track wayward souls across the wastes that flee from their dark fates, and are one of the only creatures that feel comfortable traversing the maw.', -1, 0),
(401305, 15, 5, 'Darkwarren Hardshell', 401305, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401305, 6, 1, 'The Darkwarren Hardshell\'s chitin is sturdy enough to withstand mortar shells and dragon\'s fire. It will also conveniently consume anything lacking anima, if needed.', -1, 0),
(401306, 15, 5, 'Swift Gloomhoof', 401306, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401306, 6, 1, 'The ballads of Ardenweald claim that the birth of gloomrunner heralds the passing of a particularly benevolent wild god. Seeing a gloomrunner is therefore a blessing and a curse.', -1, 0),
(401307, 15, 5, 'Sundancer', 401307, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401307, 6, 1, 'This sun-dappled courser gallops on lightbeams with carefree abandon.', -1, 0),
(401309, 15, 5, 'Chittering Animite', 401309, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401309, 6, 1, 'These exceptionally agile fliers make excellent mounts once they\'ve been trained not to sap every ounce of anima from their rider.', -1, 0),
(401310, 15, 5, 'Horrid Dredwing', 401310, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401310, 6, 1, 'Harika the Horrid terrorized the denizens of the Forest Ward, and with her demise her broodlings can now take this horror to denizens farther afield.', -1, 0),
(401311, 15, 5, 'Ivory Cloud Serpent', 401311, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401311, 6, 1, 'Ivory Cloud Serpents are often mistaken for roaring thunder as they tear through the skies with blistering speed.', -1, 0),
(401312, 15, 5, 'Gargantuan Grrloc', 401312, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401312, 6, 1, 'It\'s the biggest murloc you\'ve ever seen!', -1, 0),
(401313, 15, 5, 'Rajani Warserpent', 401313, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401313, 6, 1, 'Fierce companions of the followers of Ra-den, the Rajani Warserpents are a force to be reckoned with.', -1, 0),
(401314, 15, 5, 'Drake of the Four Winds', 401314, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401314, 6, 1, 'Rocks erode, fires sputter, but wind remains powerful regardless of the passage of time. -Phaoris', -1, 0),
(401315, 15, 5, 'Mail Muncher', 401315, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401315, 6, 1, 'Worming its way through the Postmaster\'s network, this serpent of N\'Zoth deprived Azeroth of its primary magical correspondence.', -1, 0),
(401317, 15, 5, 'Waste Marauder', 401317, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401317, 6, 1, 'Larger than most of its kin, this vulture has shown sick and strong beasts alike why they need to fear the skies.', -1, 0),
(401318, 15, 5, 'Wastewander Skyterror', 401318, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401318, 6, 1, 'Doubting a Wastewander Skyterror\'s capabilities is a quick way to find yourself missing a limb.', -1, 0),
(401319, 15, 5, 'Malevolent Drone', 401319, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401319, 6, 1, 'The Aqir drones feast on heroes and cowards alike to grow their ranks.', -1, 0),
(401320, 15, 5, 'Shadowbarb Drone', 401320, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401320, 6, 1, 'Void, jelly, and a very full belly is all this drone needs.', -1, 0),
(401321, 15, 5, 'Wicked Swarmer', 401321, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401321, 6, 1, 'When the Void reached out, the Aqir were formed in its terrible image.', -1, 0),
(401322, 15, 5, 'Wriggling Parasite', 401322, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401322, 6, 1, 'It\'s so wiggly! Just looking at it move is chaotic and unnerving.', -1, 0),
(401324, 15, 5, 'Elusive Quickhoof', 401324, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401324, 6, 1, 'The kind nature of alpacas makes them perfect as companions for the intrepid adventurer.', -1, 0),
(401326, 15, 5, 'Awakened Mindborer', 401326, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401326, 6, 1, 'It may look menacing right now, but it\'s actually kind of cute when it\'s asleep.', -1, 0),
(401327, 15, 5, 'Ren\'s Stalwart Hound', 401327, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401327, 6, 1, 'Houndlord Ren used his strongest quilen to carry him across Pandaria to subjugate the Vale for the Mogu empire.', -1, 0),
(401328, 15, 5, 'Xinlao', 401328, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401328, 6, 1, 'The only thing stronger than a quilen\'s loyalty is its fierce devotion to making sure it covers its owner in kisses.', -1, 0),
(401329, 15, 5, 'Springfur Alpaca', 401329, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401329, 6, 1, 'The kind nature of alpacas makes them perfect as companions for the intrepid adventurer.', -1, 0),
(401330, 15, 5, 'Sunwarmed Furline', 401330, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401330, 6, 1, 'The presence of the giant felines heralds the beginning of the end for the birds of Azeroth.', -1, 0),
(401332, 15, 5, 'Silky Shimmermoth', 401332, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401332, 6, 1, 'The moths of Ardenweald play a vital role in the ecosystem, carrying spores, anima, and pollen from one part of the forest to the other, providing nourishment and variation to the denizens living below.', -1, 0),
(401346, 15, 5, 'Steamscale Incinerator', 401346, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401346, 6, 1, 'A mad gnomish inventor had a dream to ride a dragon, so he created this metal monstrosity. He powered it with a trapped demon, in order to create "an authentic dragon soul," and did not survive its activation.', -1, 0),
(401350, 15, 5, 'Colossal Slaughterclaw', 401350, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401350, 6, 1, 'Only the most stalwart stable masters of Maldraxxus are able to break the will of the colossal slaughterclaws, giving all champions of the Undying Army a fearsome ally in the Shadowlands.', -1, 0),
(401351, 15, 5, 'Vicious War Spider', 401351, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401351, 6, 1, 'When being a courageous member of the Alliance doesn\'t strike the right amount of fear into your opponent, add a giant spider.', -1, 0),
(401352, 15, 5, 'Vicious War Spider', 401352, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401352, 6, 1, 'When being a bellowing member of the Horde doesn\'t strike the right amount of fear into your opponent, add a giant spider.', -1, 0),
(401354, 15, 5, 'Shadeleaf Runestag', 401354, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401354, 6, 1, 'The shadeleaf runestag are bred for their ferocity as well as their beauty by the Wild Hunt. They feel no fear charging into the den of any predator.', -1, 0),
(401355, 15, 5, 'Wakener\'s Runestag', 401355, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401355, 6, 1, 'Runestags enjoy lying near wildseeds. The Wakeners believe they can hear the sleepers\' dreams. These runestags display a range of emotions in their vigil, signaling the dreams or nightmares of the spirits within.', -1, 0),
(401356, 15, 5, 'Winterborn Runestag', 401356, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401356, 6, 1, 'Winterborn runestags are blessed by the Winter Queen herself. Their runes flare brilliantly when predators are nearby, warning the entire herd.', -1, 0),
(401357, 15, 5, 'Enchanted Shadeleaf Runestag', 401357, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401357, 6, 1, 'A shadeleaf runestag is capable of goring creatures as powerful as a gorm matriarch in defense of its herd.', -1, 0),
(401358, 15, 5, 'Enchanted Wakener\'s Runestag', 401358, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401358, 6, 1, 'Wakener runestags fiercely protect their wildseed groves. When the groves starting to fail, many runestags went berserk.', -1, 0),
(401359, 15, 5, 'Enchanted Winterborn Runestag', 401359, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401359, 6, 1, 'Winterborn runestags are the favored mount of the Winter Queen herself, and she only bestows such a creature on her most favored subjects.', -1, 0),
(401360, 15, 5, 'Shimmermist Runner', 401360, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401360, 6, 1, 'Mischievous spriggans and the valerunners have a natural enmity. No valerunner would deign to allow a spriggan rider because they can sense their inherent malevolence.', -1, 0),
(401361, 15, 5, 'Duskflutter Ardenmoth', 401361, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401361, 6, 1, 'These ardenmoths prefer the dark and damp forests of northwest Ardenweald, where fungal colonies are perpetually blooming.', -1, 0),
(401362, 15, 5, 'Spinemaw Gladechewer', 401362, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401362, 6, 1, 'Spriggan riders tie bits of anima-less detritus to the end of sticks in front of their gorm mounts to steer. It\'s... an imperfect art.', -1, 0),
(401363, 15, 5, 'Sinful Gladiator\'s Soul Eater', 401363, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401363, 6, 1, 'This mount shows a proclivity for snacking upon the souls cast out of Revendreth.', -1, 0),
(401364, 15, 5, 'War-Bred Tauralus', 401364, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401364, 6, 1, 'The soldiers of Maldraxxus protect the Shadowlands, and require a mount that is both capable and calm when faced with overwhelming odds.', -1, 0),
(401365, 15, 5, 'Plaguerot Tauralus', 401365, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401365, 6, 1, 'The tauralus is considered courageous, though scholars of Maldraxxus have long wondered if their lack of fear is simply due to the tiny size of their brains.', -1, 0),
(401366, 15, 5, 'Bonehoof Tauralus', 401366, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401366, 6, 1, 'There are quite a few reasons that you do not want to stand behind a tauralus, the hooves and whip-like tails being the least of them.', -1, 0),
(401367, 15, 5, 'Chosen Tauralus', 401367, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401367, 6, 1, 'Even an unarmored tauralus is a valuable ally in battle, its enormous horns capable of piercing even plate armor.', -1, 0),
(401368, 15, 5, 'Armored War-Bred Tauralus', 401368, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401368, 6, 1, 'The tauralus that serve the armies of Maldraxxus have had all traits of compassion bred out of them, and are only adorned in armor when they show that no sword or spell can stop them from carrying their rider to victory.', -1, 0),
(401369, 15, 5, 'Armored Plaguerot Tauralus', 401369, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401369, 6, 1, 'When fully armored, a tauralus can take an incredible amount of damage before falling, making it a valuable ally in battle.', -1, 0),
(401370, 15, 5, 'Armored Bonehoof Tauralus', 401370, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401370, 6, 1, 'A favored mount of the House of the Chosen, the tauralus only gets more angry and vicious when exposed to battle.', -1, 0),
(401371, 15, 5, 'Armored Chosen Tauralus', 401371, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401371, 6, 1, 'The tauralus has two tails, which are both absolutely necessary for whipping away buzzing pests like the bloodlouse.', -1, 0),
(401372, 15, 5, 'Blisterback Bloodtusk', 401372, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401372, 6, 1, 'The House of the Chosen train their mounts in all manner of difficult circumstances, so that no matter the battle, they will never falter.', -1, 0),
(401373, 15, 5, 'Gorespine', 401373, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401373, 6, 1, 'Nerissa trampled over countless bodies on the back of Gorespine as she rose to prominence as the commander of the Lichsworn forces for the House of Rituals.', -1, 0),
(401374, 15, 5, 'Bonecleaver\'s Skullboar', 401374, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401374, 6, 1, 'Sabreil was known for the ruthless efficiency with which she dismembered foes, feeding their bones to her loyal skullboar.', -1, 0),
(401375, 15, 5, 'Lurid Bloodtusk', 401375, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401375, 6, 1, 'Only bloodtusks that survive the Contest of Conquest are deemed worthy enough to become a mount of the Undying Army.', -1, 0),
(401376, 15, 5, 'Silvertip Dredwing', 401376, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401376, 6, 1, 'Bred by the Revendreth prince, Renathal, these rare dredwing are fiercely loyal and will only let those deemed worthy by the prince himself to interact with them.', -1, 0),
(401377, 15, 5, 'Rampart Screecher', 401377, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401377, 6, 1, 'Roosting among the ramparts of Castle Nathria, these giant dredbats act as sentinels and are trained to take down threats approaching the castle from the air.', -1, 0),
(401378, 15, 5, 'Harvester\'s Dredwing', 401378, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401378, 6, 1, 'The dredwings of the Harvesters fear no mawsworn, and will gleefully sink their teeth into anything that threatens Sinfall.', -1, 0),
(401379, 15, 5, 'Endmire Flyer', 401379, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401379, 6, 1, 'Attracted through portals through which little is known these flying devourers have found a home in the Endmire of Revendreth feeding on the latent anima.', -1, 0),
(401382, 15, 5, 'Inquisition Gargon', 401382, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401382, 6, 1, 'The gargon of the Inquisitors are some of the most vicious ever carved. The Avowed seek to recapture these beasts and return them to the righteous duty of assisting in the purifying of souls rather than the perversions performed at the hands of the Inq...', -1, 0),
(401384, 15, 5, 'Sinfall Gargon', 401384, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401384, 6, 1, 'The gargon are the loyal mounts and companions of the Venthyr and Renathal has found many abandoned at Sinfall, awaiting reawakening and assignment to worthy members of the covenant.', -1, 0),
(401385, 15, 5, 'Crypt Gargon', 401385, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401385, 6, 1, 'Loyal hounds of the Curator, these gargon patrol the crypts and catacombs deterring both trespassing and escape.', -1, 0),
(401387, 15, 5, 'Desire\'s Battle Gargon', 401387, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401387, 6, 1, 'The Countess maintains a small stable of elegantly adorned gargon mounts for her sole use. Many a rival has been taken in by the finery to their peril as she personally oversees their deadly training.', -1, 0),
(401388, 15, 5, 'Gravestone Battle Gargon', 401388, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401388, 6, 1, 'Representative of a new loyal batch of gargon, these battle ready beasts will take Renathal\'s most loyal compatriots into the final battles against the Jailer.', -1, 0),
(401389, 15, 5, 'Battle Gargon Silessa', 401389, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401389, 6, 1, 'Silessa fought valiantly alongside her master in the great incursion by the Light, following the battle her master set her to guard over a vault room of great value.', -1, 0),
(401391, 15, 5, 'Loyal Gorger', 401391, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401391, 6, 1, 'Crawling forth from the cracks between the realms, the devourers have a voracious appetite for anima. Little is known of their origins, but all denizens of the Shadowlands see their recent boldness as a sign of the end times.', -1, 0),
(401392, 15, 5, 'Pale Acidmaw', 401392, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401392, 6, 1, 'The acid present in the ichor of this creature sapped away the color from its shell, leaving it a striking shade of snowy white.', -1, 0),
(401393, 15, 5, 'Wild Glimmerfur Prowler', 401393, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401393, 6, 1, 'This prowler\'s brilliant green coat distinguishes it from the blues and purples of Ardenweald, making it much easier for others of its kind to see through the midnight woods.', -1, 0),
(401394, 15, 5, 'Phalynx of Loyalty', 401394, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401394, 6, 1, 'Some within the Ascended keep a phalynx as a pet. While they may not be as furry as a larion, they are much less likely to eat your other pets.', -1, 0),
(401395, 15, 5, 'Phalynx of Humility', 401395, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401395, 6, 1, 'The phalynx does not fetch, though it is not known why this is.', -1, 0),
(401396, 15, 5, 'Phalynx of Courage', 401396, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401396, 6, 1, 'A phalynx is considered both a worthy companion and a lithe opponent to test one\'s reflexes against.', -1, 0),
(401397, 15, 5, 'Wildseed Cradle', 401397, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401397, 6, 1, 'The most precious cargo in all Ardenweald, the wildseeds, are cradled by this lovingly-crafted cart. It is imbued with anima to allow it to hover over the ground.', -1, 0),
(401398, 15, 5, 'Phalynx of Purity', 401398, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401398, 6, 1, 'Little is known about the origination of phalynx technology, the machinations of which are taught more akin to religion than engineering.', -1, 0),
(401399, 15, 5, 'Eternal Phalynx of Purity', 401399, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401399, 6, 1, 'The armored phalynx is a favorite companion of the mightiest warriors of the Ascended as it is both fearless and vicious in battle.', -1, 0),
(401400, 15, 5, 'Eternal Phalynx of Courage', 401400, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401400, 6, 1, 'Many bars of gildenite are required to forge one of these sparkling mounts, but the sight of them alone is worth the gathering time.', -1, 0),
(401401, 15, 5, 'Eternal Phalynx of Loyalty', 401401, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401401, 6, 1, 'A marvel of steward engineering, the armored phalynx is a rare and awe-inspiring sight.', -1, 0),
(401402, 15, 5, 'Eternal Phalynx of Humility', 401402, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401402, 6, 1, 'When an armored phalynx is forged, stewards clap their hammers together in reverence of the skill required in its creation.', -1, 0),
(401404, 15, 5, 'Silverwind Larion', 401404, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401404, 6, 1, 'This gift of the silvery winds is only bestowed upon those that search high and low for the wisdom of Bastion.', -1, 0),
(401405, 15, 5, 'Restoration Deathwalker', 401405, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401405, 6, 1, 'With the death of the Jailer and the ascension of a new Arbiter, the Shadowlands is returning to its great Purpose. Some deathwalkers recognize the role that mortal heroes have played, and are willing to serve as mounts.', -1, 0),
(401406, 15, 5, 'Marrowfang', 401406, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401406, 6, 1, 'Marrowfang, Bonefang\'s progeny, was respected by Amarth the Harvester for her insatiable appetite, even if it disrupted any experiments that the sadistic commander wanted to run.', -1, 0),
(401407, 15, 5, 'Callow Flayedwing', 401407, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401407, 6, 1, 'Flayedwings are a necessary force in the cycle of life for the Shadowlands, acting as both prey and predator for the harsh environment of Maldraxxus.', -1, 0),
(401408, 15, 5, 'Gruesome Flayedwing', 401408, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401408, 6, 1, 'The flayedwings of Maldraxxus are prized for their ability to soar effortlessly through the skies of the Shadowlands, allowing their rider a surprise opportunity to strike at their foes or support their allies.', -1, 0),
(401409, 15, 5, 'Bonesewn Fleshroc', 401409, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401409, 6, 1, 'Only expert flesh-stitchers who have demonstrated mastery over the magics of Maldraxxus are powerful enough to construct a deathroc of this size.', -1, 0),
(401410, 15, 5, 'Hulking Deathroc', 401410, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401410, 6, 1, 'Deathrocs are stitched monstrosities from the discarded viscera, bone, and organs that were not required to construct soldiers for the House of Constructs.', -1, 0),
(401411, 15, 5, 'Predatory Plagueroc', 401411, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401411, 6, 1, 'Gieger\'s everlasting hunger is legendary amongst the House of Constructs, and no beast is too large or bony to fit inside its massive stomach.', -1, 0),
(401413, 15, 5, 'Dauntless Duskrunner', 401413, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401413, 6, 1, 'The Path of Ascension is a challenging trial, and those that display all of the facets the Kyrian hold dear will be duly rewarded.', -1, 0),
(401414, 15, 5, 'Sinrunner Blanchy', 401414, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401414, 6, 1, 'In life, Blanchy appeared to be an affectionate, well-behaved horse of excellent disposition and appetite. What evils must she have committed in secret to have earned her place among the condemned souls of Revendreth?', -1, 0),
(401415, 15, 5, 'Arboreal Gulper', 401415, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401415, 6, 1, 'The wood and foliage growing atop this toad is a natural part of its body, helping it siphon anima from the air to nourish itself.', -1, 0),
(401416, 15, 5, 'Mawsworn Charger', 401416, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401416, 6, 1, 'The fate of all horse mounts.', -1, 0),
(401417, 15, 5, 'Hand of Hrestimorak', 401417, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401417, 6, 1, 'The treachery of Hrestimorak was infamous, betraying his people to claim power. Facing damnation in the Maw, he tried to subvert the Jailer... a foolish act that would earn him an eternity of torment.', -1, 0),
(401419, 15, 5, 'Sintouched Deathwalker', 401419, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401419, 6, 1, 'Forged from the sins of countless diabolical dungeon denizens. Only those with the skills to overcome them may hold its reins.', -1, 0),
(401420, 15, 5, 'Umbral Scythehorn', 401420, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401420, 6, 1, 'Umbral gorm are the most docile of all gorm, but they also grow the largest horns and mandibles. They are probably so docile because other creatures avoid riling them.', -1, 0),
(401421, 15, 5, 'Court Sinrunner', 401421, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401421, 6, 1, 'Sinrunners were once the steeds of dark souls, carried in the wake of either their sins or their masters\' sins to Revendreth. While some chose to run free, many continue to serve darkness in death as they did in life.', -1, 0),
(401422, 15, 5, 'Warstitched Darkhound', 401422, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401422, 6, 1, 'These warhounds are crafted by the House of Constructs to carry any rider into the thick of battle, rending and tearing enemy mounts all the while.', -1, 0),
(401423, 15, 5, 'Highwind Darkmane', 401423, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401423, 6, 1, 'The Forsworn and their mounts take on a darker aspect upon renouncing the path laid forth by the Archon. While tame enough to ride, the Highwind Darkmane has a fiercely independent streak.', -1, 0),
(401424, 15, 5, 'Snowstorm', 401424, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401424, 6, 1, 'He comes from the ice and snow, under the Azeroth sun where adventurers go.', -1, 0),
(401425, 15, 5, 'Gilded Prowler', 401425, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401425, 6, 1, 'The mighty larion is an apex predator of Bastion, but that does not stop it from enjoying a nice nap in the sunny fields.', -1, 0),
(401426, 15, 5, 'Ascended Skymane', 401426, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401426, 6, 1, 'Only those that have proven themselves against the combined might of the Ascended will be able to ride this mount.', -1, 0),
(401428, 15, 5, 'Amber Ardenmoth', 401428, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401428, 6, 1, 'The brilliant orange hue of the amber ardenmoth signals to predators that it is dangerous to eat. Consuming one of these creatures will put a predator into a dreamless sleep for years.', -1, 0),
(401429, 15, 5, 'Vibrant Flutterwing', 401429, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401429, 6, 1, 'These minty green moths are very friendly. They particularly enjoy having their head fuzz vigorously brushed. They also enjoy music and poetry.', -1, 0),
(401430, 15, 5, 'Desertwing Hunter', 401430, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401430, 6, 1, 'In service of the great Purpose, desertwing hunters were designed to fill distant skies of forgotten realms of the Shadowlands.', -1, 0),
(401431, 15, 5, 'Pale Regal Cervid', 401431, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401431, 6, 1, 'Looking at these majestic creatures, it\'s not difficult to see how the idea of cervids developed into the stags found on Azeroth and other mortal worlds.', -1, 0),
(401433, 15, 5, 'Vespoid Flutterer', 401433, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401433, 6, 1, 'A flutterer is an overgrown vespoid worker created to carry a rider. Rather than looking to a queen for leadership, it looks to its rider to guide it in all things.', -1, 0),
(401434, 15, 5, 'Deepstar Aurelid', 401434, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401434, 6, 1, 'As one of the last remaining polyps of an elusive creature, this aurelid is at home in the water as much as the air.', -1, 0),
(401436, 15, 5, 'Battle-Hardened Aquilon', 401436, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401436, 6, 1, 'The aquilon can be a valuable ally in combat, with capabilities exceeding those of the phalynx.', -1, 0),
(401437, 15, 5, 'Battle-Bound Warhound', 401437, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401437, 6, 1, 'Warhounds find comfort in conflict, and the Contest of Conquest is the perfect place to find these beasts honing their abilities.', -1, 0),
(401438, 15, 5, 'Bulbous Necroray', 401438, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401438, 6, 1, 'The necrorays of Maldraxxus prefer to congregate around the enormous decaying mushrooms of the region.', -1, 0),
(401439, 15, 5, 'Infested Necroray', 401439, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401439, 6, 1, 'Necrorays lay their eggs in small clusters within the frills and hollows of decaying fungal blooms.', -1, 0),
(401440, 15, 5, 'Pestilent Necroray', 401440, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401440, 6, 1, 'When a necroray hatches, spores fly everywhere, making a huge mess.', -1, 0),
(401441, 15, 5, 'Bound Shadehound', 401441, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401441, 6, 1, 'Created by deciphering and performing powerful runic magic, this Shadehound is bound to its creator.', -1, 0),
(401442, 15, 5, 'Corridor Creeper', 401442, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401442, 6, 1, 'The loyal hounds of the Jailer creep along the corridors in search of the scent of souls.', -1, 0),
(401443, 15, 5, 'Voracious Gorger', 401443, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401443, 6, 1, 'The devourers are presumed to have their origins in the In-Between, a space between the lands of the Shadowlands that few have explored.', -1, 0),
(401444, 15, 5, 'Viridian Phase-Hunter', 401444, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401444, 6, 1, 'Hailing from a species already adept at natural camouflage, the otherworldly energies that transformed Draenor into Outland gave these creatures the ability to shift through space.', -1, 0),
(401445, 15, 5, 'Slime Serpent', 401445, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401445, 6, 1, 'This mysterious creature lurks beneath the slime pools of Plaguefall. No one knows where it came from.', -1, 0),
(401446, 15, 5, 'Tazavesh Gearglider', 401446, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401446, 6, 1, 'Brokers of all types use these gliders to travel around Tazavesh and similar nearby outposts, and carry their goods as well.', -1, 0),
(401448, 15, 5, 'Serenade', 401448, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401448, 6, 1, 'These beautiful helicids emerge only at night. When they are pleased, their shells hum with a joyful melody.', -1, 0),
(401449, 15, 5, 'Lord of the Corpseflies', 401449, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401449, 6, 1, 'To be the Lord of the Corpseflies, you\'ve got to lay a LOT of eggs.', -1, 0),
(401450, 15, 5, 'Soaring Razorwing', 401450, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401450, 6, 1, 'The hide of the razorwing is light, allowing it to fly, but also quite tough, allowing them to survive passage into the Maw.', -1, 0),
(401451, 15, 5, 'Vicious War Croaker', 401451, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401451, 6, 1, 'These creatures are so enthusiastic when charging into battle that they will croak out something that sounds very much like "FOR THE HORDE!"', -1, 0),
(401452, 15, 5, 'Vicious War Croaker', 401452, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401452, 6, 1, 'These creatures are so enthusiastic when charging into battle that they will croak out something that sounds very much like "FOR THE ALLIANCE!"', -1, 0),
(401454, 15, 5, 'Tamed Mauler', 401454, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401454, 6, 1, 'When it comes to taming devourers, all it takes is a little anima and a lot of patience. And a lot of healing potions.', -1, 0),
(401455, 15, 5, 'Beryl Shardhide', 401455, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401455, 6, 1, 'These shardhides find it easy to hide in the underbrush, and it is rare to find one that is tamed.', -1, 0),
(401456, 15, 5, 'Sapphire Skyblazer', 401456, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401456, 6, 1, 'These brilliant blue birds burn brighter (and hotter) than their orange cousins, though the origin of both remains a mystery.', -1, 0),
(401458, 15, 5, 'Wandering Ancient', 401458, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401458, 6, 1, 'A staunch defender of the forests of Azeroth, the ancients are also known for their glorious canopies of leaves, which change color with the seasons.', -1, 0),
(401459, 15, 5, 'Vicious War Gorm', 401459, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401459, 6, 1, 'The gorm love eating the corpses of your enemies, so this seemed like a natural fit.', -1, 0),
(401460, 15, 5, 'Vicious War Gorm', 401460, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401460, 6, 1, 'The gorm love eating the corpses of your enemies, so this seemed like a natural fit.', -1, 0),
(401465, 15, 5, 'Vicious Warstalker', 401465, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401465, 6, 1, 'Trample the Horde to dust while riding a majestic protoform wolf! For the Alliance!', -1, 0),
(401466, 15, 5, 'Vicious Warstalker', 401466, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401466, 6, 1, 'Trample the Alliance to dust while riding a majestic protoform wolf! For the Horde!', -1, 0),
(401467, 15, 5, 'Noble Bruffalon', 401467, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401467, 6, 1, 'It is a great honor to be trusted with one of the Maruuk\'s loyal hunting companions. This Bruffalon is reliable and steadfast through any hardship.', -1, 0),
(401468, 15, 5, 'Amber Skitterfly', 401468, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401468, 6, 1, 'A gift from Granpap Whiskers to the Trading Post, amber skitterflies are remarkably docile.', -1, 0),
(401469, 15, 5, 'Magmashell', 401469, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401469, 6, 1, 'Who\'s a good little new-forged snail made entirely of elemental lava? You are! Yes, you!', -1, 0),
(401470, 15, 5, 'Liquid Hot Magma Slug', 401470, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401470, 6, 1, 'Also referred to as lava slugs once they breach Azeroth\'s crust.', -1, 0),
(401471, 15, 5, 'Vengeance', 401471, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401471, 6, 1, 'Sylvanas lost a part of herself the day Arthas took her life, and the darkness within her grew to fill the void.', -1, 0),
(401474, 15, 5, 'Bestowed Thunderspine Packleader', 401474, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401474, 6, 1, 'A gift from Merithra, who blessed these thunderspines to ensure that no matter where the Maruuk clans roam, they will always be under the green dragonflight\'s protection.', -1, 0),
(401475, 15, 5, 'Hand of Bahmethra', 401475, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401475, 6, 1, 'The most wicked and cruel of her kin, Bahmethra endured the full measure of the Banished One\'s punishments before her fall.', -1, 0),
(401476, 15, 5, 'Wild Hunt Legsplitter', 401476, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401476, 6, 1, 'Integrated into the depleted forces of the Wild Hunt, the fawn riders quickly found that the gorm\'s powerful mandibles were perfect for cutting down close enemy ranks.', -1, 0),
(401477, 15, 5, 'Undying Darkhound', 401477, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401477, 6, 1, 'The Undying Darkhound\'s parts have graced many battlefields, yet this latest battle may have been the first time they all fought together.', -1, 0),
(401478, 15, 5, 'Skyskin Hornstrider', 401478, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401478, 6, 1, 'The instability of primalist storms in potential timelines sometimes causes creatures to absorb the energies from the very storms. These creatures tend to be docile towards those who are able to face the fury of these chronomatic anomalies.', -1, 0),
(401480, 15, 5, 'Unchained Gladiator\'s Soul Eater', 401480, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401480, 6, 1, 'This soul eater\'s gaze unnerves you. Best not meet its eyes for too long.', -1, 0),
(401481, 15, 5, 'Cartel Master\'s Gearglider', 401481, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401481, 6, 1, 'Only the richest cartel leaders are able to afford the metals required to craft the Cartel Master\'s Gearglider.', -1, 0),
(401482, 15, 5, 'Xy Trustee\'s Gearglider', 401482, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401482, 6, 1, 'Cartel Xy trades in many currencies; none are as valuable to its inner circle as loyalty.', -1, 0),
(401483, 15, 5, 'Vandal\'s Gearglider', 401483, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401483, 6, 1, 'A rarer, customized glider most commonly used for clandestine gatherings. Its silence makes it near impossible to detect, making it a favored tool for those who work in the shadows.', -1, 0),
(401484, 15, 5, 'Ardenweald Wilderling', 401484, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401484, 6, 1, 'As anima flows to the distant wealds of Ardenweald once more, the wilderlings awaken and cautiously emerge from their canopy burrows.', -1, 0),
(401485, 15, 5, 'Autumnal Wilderling', 401485, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401485, 6, 1, 'The wilderlings are benevolent, magical creatures of Ardenweald, and are drawn to souls that are strong and pure.', -1, 0),
(401486, 15, 5, 'Winter Wilderling', 401486, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401486, 6, 1, 'Wilderlings serve as support units in battle, preserving their allies and rendering enemy magics useless.', -1, 0),
(401487, 15, 5, 'Summer Wilderling', 401487, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401487, 6, 1, 'Stubborn and rebellious, this wilderling is loyal to very few. But those few are bonded for life.', -1, 0),
(401489, 15, 5, 'Obsidian Gravewing', 401489, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401489, 6, 1, 'In the darkened skies of Revendreth, you cannot see these creatures coming until it is too late.', -1, 0),
(401490, 15, 5, 'Sinfall Gravewing', 401490, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401490, 6, 1, 'With anima once again flowing in Sinfall, the Stonewright has been able to infuse these Stoneborn, making them valuable allies in the battles to come.', -1, 0),
(401491, 15, 5, 'Pale Gravewing', 401491, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401491, 6, 1, 'Gravewings know no fear and are nearly indestructible -- perfect for an assault on the Maw.', -1, 0),
(401492, 15, 5, 'Elysian Aquilon', 401492, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401492, 6, 1, 'With anima once again flowing to the Eternal Forge in Bastion, the plans for the aquilon centurion could be crafted once more.', -1, 0),
(401493, 15, 5, 'Forsworn Aquilon', 401493, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401493, 6, 1, 'Originally produced by the Forsworn with stolen blueprints, these powerful centurion are now earning a reputation across the Shadowlands.', -1, 0),
(401494, 15, 5, 'Ascendant\'s Aquilon', 401494, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401494, 6, 1, 'The aquilon can rapidly transport aspirants, stewards, and even ascended to a location. Hey, sometimes your wings get tired.', -1, 0),
(401495, 15, 5, 'Maldraxxian Corpsefly', 401495, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401495, 6, 1, 'Corpseflies were once found throughout Maldraxxus, but many died out in the absence of anima. With anima flowing once again, they swarm.', -1, 0),
(401496, 15, 5, 'Regal Corpsefly', 401496, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401496, 6, 1, 'Only the forces of Maldraxxus would call a corpsefly "regal."', -1, 0),
(401497, 15, 5, 'Battlefield Swarmer', 401497, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401497, 6, 1, 'Corpseflies are strongly attracted to the smell of dead bodies and will swarm an active battlefield as soon as the first corpse falls.', -1, 0),
(401500, 15, 5, 'Sanctum Gloomcharger', 401500, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401500, 6, 1, 'Only the Jailer\'s most powerful lieutenants are gifted these steeds to stalk the halls of the Tower.', -1, 0),
(401501, 15, 5, 'Soulbound Gloomcharger', 401501, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401501, 6, 1, 'Ve\'nari has many methods of sneaking around the Maw and disrupting the Jailer\'s plans, including binding his own minions.', -1, 0),
(401502, 15, 5, 'Fallen Charger', 401502, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401502, 6, 1, 'The charger\'s screams echo across the Maw as it continues a never-ending ride across the land, forever looking for escape from the endless torments it has been forced to endure.', -1, 0),
(401503, 15, 5, 'Hand of Nilganihmaht', 401503, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401503, 6, 1, 'Of all the giants who dared defy the Jailer, Nilganihmaht was the most arrogant. For this transgression, the giant\'s severed hand was hidden within a veil of torments, and the rings that could summon it back were scattered across the Maw.', -1, 0),
(401504, 15, 5, 'Hand of Salaranga', 401504, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401504, 6, 1, 'Salaranga was the most cunning of her kin and hid amongst the Beastwarrens. She struck at the Banished One with a horde of bestial allies. It did not matter.', -1, 0),
(401505, 15, 5, 'Amber Shardhide', 401505, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401505, 6, 1, 'The bright colors of Korthian wildlife indicate that they have either few predators, or are tough enough to fight back.', -1, 0),
(401506, 15, 5, 'Crimson Shardhide', 401506, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401506, 6, 1, 'When Korthia was pulled into The Maw, only a few hardy species survived.', -1, 0),
(401507, 15, 5, 'Darkmaul', 401507, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401507, 6, 1, 'An older shardhide, Darkmaul was relatively tame and friendly around Korthians. He was thought lost to the calamity.', -1, 0),
(401508, 15, 5, 'Fierce Razorwing', 401508, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401508, 6, 1, 'Razorwings generally stay away from other Korthian species, but with time and patience, they can be tamed as well.', -1, 0),
(401509, 15, 5, 'Garnet Razorwing', 401509, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401509, 6, 1, 'Korthia was once known for its bright red flowers. Several species were known for consuming or rolling in them, and taking on bright red coloration as a result.', -1, 0),
(401510, 15, 5, 'Dusklight Razorwing', 401510, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401510, 6, 1, 'Razorwings can be seen throughout Korthia, making their nests on high hills and in trees.', -1, 0),
(401511, 15, 5, 'Maelie, the Wanderer', 401511, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401511, 6, 1, 'A curious and inquisitive doe, she doesn\'t mean to worry her master, she just gets distracted easily. Especially with all of the new things to see on Korthia.', -1, 0),
(401513, 15, 5, 'Sarge\'s Tale', 401513, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401513, 6, 1, 'Hold on a sec, Sarge isn\'t that large, someone must have spun a tall tale in the Hearthstone Tavern...', -1, 0),
(401514, 15, 5, 'Rampaging Mauler', 401514, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401514, 6, 1, 'One would think controlling a rampaging mount would be difficult, but if you can learn to control the direction of the rampage it can be quite useful.', -1, 0),
(401517, 15, 5, 'Bound Blizzard', 401517, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401517, 6, 1, 'A flurrious, fridgid friend, frost-flecked for frozen fun.', -1, 0),
(401520, 15, 5, 'Soultwisted Deathwalker', 401520, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401520, 6, 1, 'A howling vortex of tormented souls, ridden only by those who wish to demonstrate their impressive tolerance for pain and suffering.', -1, 0),
(401521, 15, 5, 'Val\'sharah Hippogryph', 401521, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401521, 6, 1, 'These majestic hippogryphs are as close to a being of the Emerald Dream as any resident of Azeroth can be, and do not bond with a rider easily.', -1, 0),
(401522, 15, 5, 'Heartlight Vombata', 401522, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401522, 6, 1, 'The Enlightened revere all creations of the First Ones, yet for many, the vombata of Zereth Mortis are the most beloved. These creatures are equal parts trusted beast of burden and beloved companion.', -1, 0),
(401523, 15, 5, 'Curious Crystalsniffer', 401523, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401523, 6, 1, 'Most vombata enjoy tunneling through the ground, but these sniffers seem to have an unerring ability to locate crystals buried deep underground and will congregate around large deposits.', -1, 0),
(401524, 15, 5, 'Darkened Vombata', 401524, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401524, 6, 1, 'The schematic to synthesize these darkened vombata seem to have appeared as a reaction to the Mawsworn invasion. The resulting vombata look different--darker, much like the invaders--but behave normally.', -1, 0),
(401525, 15, 5, 'Adorned Vombata', 401525, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401525, 6, 1, 'Red-colored vombata are considered lucky by the Enlightened. It was a red vombata that was present when they first arrived in Zereth Mortis.', -1, 0),
(401526, 15, 5, 'Deathrunner', 401526, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401526, 6, 1, 'These wild cervids are only truly at peace when running through--or between--the lands of Death.', -1, 0),
(401528, 15, 5, 'Sundered Zerethsteed', 401528, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401528, 6, 1, 'Whatever the purpose of these cervids once was, it is long forgotten. Though they are not Dominated, they have been corrupted by the unintended presence of Mawsworn in the sacred realm of Zereth Mortis.', -1, 0),
(401529, 15, 5, 'Anointed Protostag', 401529, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401529, 6, 1, 'Only those most esteemed by the Enlightened are trusted with the reins of this rare cervid.', -1, 0),
(401531, 15, 5, 'Wen Lo, the River\'s Edge', 401531, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401531, 6, 1, 'The rivers of Pandaria, like Wen Lo, are unpredictable in nature. They may remain calm, bringing water to the crops, or flood, bringing ruin. Wen Lo reminds us that we must adapt to the challenges of life.', -1, 0),
(401532, 15, 5, 'Soaring Spelltome', 401532, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401532, 6, 1, 'In the forgotten depths of the Dalaran library, this oversized tome was found flapping madly around the room. Open the pages of this arcane-infused book and hitch a ride to magical adventure.', -1, 0),
(401533, 15, 5, 'Forged Spiteflyer', 401533, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401533, 6, 1, 'There\'s nothing that can make you feel as alive quite like riding through the realm of Death while atop a being that hates you.', -1, 0),
(401534, 15, 5, 'Buzz', 401534, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401534, 6, 1, 'Buzz buzz buzz, buzz buzz! Buzz buzz buzz buzz buzz. Buzz buzz buzz, buzz buzz buzz.', -1, 0),
(401535, 15, 5, 'Bronzewing Vespoid', 401535, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401535, 6, 1, 'Bronzewing vespoids are the result of attempting to synthesize a vespoid queen with no other members of a new hive. While no mortal has yet discovered how to synthesize a hive, the bronzewings are reliable mounts just as they are.', -1, 0),
(401536, 15, 5, 'Mawdapted Raptora', 401536, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401536, 6, 1, 'Since the Jailer\'s incursion, new raptora have been synthesized by Zereth Mortis that are capable of resisting the corrupting influence of the Maw.', -1, 0),
(401537, 15, 5, 'Raptora Swooper', 401537, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401537, 6, 1, 'The raptora swooper is one of the most vicious iterations of its kind, perfectly suited for its ecological niche. Needing no further adjustments, the ones synthesized today are identical to those created in the past.', -1, 0),
(401538, 15, 5, 'Bronze Helicid', 401538, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401538, 6, 1, 'Some helicids of Zereth Mortis have strangely metallic shells. The ones who do are generally a bronze color, indistinct from the metal any novice miner could work, save that this creature\'s construction far surpasses the skill of any novice.', -1, 0),
(401539, 15, 5, 'Unsuccessful Prototype Fleetpod', 401539, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401539, 6, 1, 'This creature was not designed by the First Ones, but instead by an unknown being attempting to create a very fast runner. Needless to say the attempt failed, because this mount is very slow.', -1, 0),
(401540, 15, 5, 'Scarlet Helicid', 401540, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401540, 6, 1, 'This helicid\'s unusual reddish tint is clearly intentional in its design, but the only other difference between these and other helicids is the unusual lack of any ooze.', -1, 0),
(401541, 15, 5, 'Genesis Crawler', 401541, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401541, 6, 1, 'The Enlightened who have observed tarachnids believe that this variety may be some of the first beings to ever walk the land of Zereth Mortis.', -1, 0),
(401542, 15, 5, 'Tarachnid Creeper', 401542, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401542, 6, 1, 'These tarachnids make their home in the darkest corners of Zereth Mortis, coming out only to hunt (or, sometimes, carry a rider around).', -1, 0),
(401543, 15, 5, 'Ineffable Skitterer', 401543, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401543, 6, 1, 'These tarachnids move with a purpose unknown to others, answering only to a higher calling. Whatever that may be, it appears to include routine assistance to mortals who need a ride. For now.', -1, 0),
(401544, 15, 5, 'Wastewarped Deathwalker', 401544, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401544, 6, 1, 'Raw swirling energy bound together into a cohesive form, it will only bend to the will of those strong enough to bind it.', -1, 0),
(401546, 15, 5, 'Iskaara Trader\'s Ottuk', 401546, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401546, 6, 1, 'There are no guarantees when you purchase an ottuk from Tattukiaka. At least they\'re cute.', -1, 0),
(401547, 15, 5, 'Goldplate Bufonid', 401547, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401547, 6, 1, 'This armored bufonid is always ready to leap into battle... as long as that battle is really, really close. In a pinch, it can leap multiple times and eventually reach the battle.', -1, 0),
(401549, 15, 5, 'Shimmering Aurelid', 401549, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401549, 6, 1, 'Though it was once created to defend the Sepulcher of the First Ones, with its primary function now completed, it now obediently follows your command.', -1, 0),
(401550, 15, 5, 'Depthstalker', 401550, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401550, 6, 1, 'Poached from Zereth Mortis, a few of these jellyfish were lost when the poachers\' ship sank. They found a new home in the Great Sea\'s depths.', -1, 0),
(401551, 15, 5, 'Cryptic Aurelid', 401551, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401551, 6, 1, 'The Cyphers of the First Ones are beyond any mortal understanding. A curious effect of the language is that, for reasons unknown, some aurelids are drawn to mortals who aspire to unlock its mystery.', -1, 0),
(401552, 15, 5, 'Carcinized Zerethsteed', 401552, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401552, 6, 1, 'The few of these mysterious creatures that remain appear to be impossibly old, almost timeless. Perhaps they were created by the First Ones, because no schematic to synthesize these has yet been discovered.', -1, 0),
(401553, 15, 5, 'Liberated Slyvern', 401553, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401553, 6, 1, 'It\'s difficult to tell because it\'s far too angry, but this slyvern is actually glad it\'s not owned by gnolls anymore.', -1, 0),
(401556, 15, 5, 'Tangled Dreamweaver', 401556, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401556, 6, 1, 'The last of the sleepers are finally awakening, bringing the dreams of the dragons back to the lands.', -1, 0),
(401563, 15, 5, 'Highland Drake', 401563, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401563, 6, 1, 'The drakes of Azure Span follow a strict personal code of honor as they explore the isles anew.', -1, 0),
(401564, 15, 5, 'Colossal Soulshredder Mawrat', 401564, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401564, 6, 1, 'The incredible prowess you have demonstrated within the Jailer\'s Tower has instilled sufficient respect into this fearsome creature, enabling its use as a mount.', -1, 0),
(401565, 15, 5, 'Colossal Umbrahide Mawrat', 401565, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401565, 6, 1, 'This disturbingly large Mawrat is an anomaly amongst its species. These Colossal Mawrats lurk only in the most distant and darkest reaches of Torghast.', -1, 0),
(401566, 15, 5, 'Colossal Ebonclaw Mawrat', 401566, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401566, 6, 1, 'This vicious and cunning creature has grown to its astonishing size by not only feasting upon the weakened souls in the Jailer\'s Tower, but also vulnerable Mawsworn.', -1, 0),
(401567, 15, 5, 'Lightforged Ruinstrider', 401567, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401567, 6, 1, '', -1, 0),
(401569, 15, 5, 'Patient Bufonid', 401569, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401569, 6, 1, 'Some bufonids will sit perfectly still for hours or days at a time if left to their own devices. Fortunately, they\'re also quite agreeable if a rider would like to move more often than that.', -1, 0),
(401570, 15, 5, 'Prototype Leaper', 401570, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401570, 6, 1, 'An ancient schematic allows for the instantiation of this early, but functional, bufonid design.', -1, 0),
(401571, 15, 5, 'Russet Bufonid', 401571, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401571, 6, 1, 'Russet is a rare color among bufonids that is normally only seen on specimens that are tainted by other cosmic forces, or synthesized from a perplexing schematic that invokes that color.', -1, 0),
(401572, 15, 5, 'Cosmic Gladiator\'s Soul Eater', 401572, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401572, 6, 1, 'This soul eater\'s gaze unnerves you. Best not meet its eyes for too long.', -1, 0),
(401573, 15, 5, 'Magenta Cloud Serpent', 401573, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401573, 6, 1, 'More affectionate than their cousins, Magenta Cloud Serpents are known to form close bonds with their riders.', -1, 0),
(401574, 15, 5, 'Crusty Crawler', 401574, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401574, 6, 1, 'This rare giant crab has taken a break from its nautical nonsense deep under the sea to explore the surface.', -1, 0),
(401575, 15, 5, 'Quawks', 401575, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401575, 6, 1, 'Squawks\'s older (and somehow louder) brother appears to tolerate your presence. For now. You should probably track down some crackers while you still can.', -1, 0),
(401576, 15, 5, 'Jigglesworth Sr.', 401576, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401576, 6, 1, 'It\'s unclear how the saddle stays atop this formerly feline friend, but somehow the House of Plagues made it work. Science.', -1, 0),
(401577, 15, 5, 'Ash\'adar, Harbinger of Dawn', 401577, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401577, 6, 1, 'Kaldorei legends whisper of a relentless hunter prowling amongst the deepest shadows of Kalimdor, never sleeping. By the light of the sun or the moon, Ash\'adar now hunts with you.', -1, 0),
(401579, 15, 5, 'Coral-Stalker Waveray', 401579, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401579, 6, 1, 'This species of ray seems to have evolved to stalk its prey amidst the brightly colored corals of the seas.', -1, 0),
(401580, 15, 5, 'Heartbond Lupine', 401580, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401580, 6, 1, 'From the moment of its creation, this packless lupine has held nothing more than deepest affection and loyalty towards you.', -1, 0),
(401581, 15, 5, 'Nether-Gorged Greatwyrm', 401581, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401581, 6, 1, 'Few mana wyrms find sufficiently stable sources of arcane power to reach such a size. A greatwyrm\'s appetite for mana is unmatched.', -1, 0),
(401582, 15, 5, 'Savage Green Battle Turtle', 401582, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401582, 6, 1, 'Turtle too slow to chase down your foes? Just add cannons. Nothing can outrun a cannon.', -1, 0),
(401583, 15, 5, 'Armored Siege Kodo', 401583, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401583, 6, 1, 'Only the strongest and most fearless of kodos can be trained to become living siege weapons. Even the highest walls won\'t keep them out for long.', -1, 0),
(401584, 15, 5, 'Colossal Plaguespew Mawrat', 401584, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401584, 6, 1, 'These rodents became Iska\'s infamous sentries, scouting and carrying her plague across the Maw. Their presence is only followed by ruin.', -1, 0),
(401585, 15, 5, 'Colossal Wraithbound Mawrat', 401585, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401585, 6, 1, 'Infused by the energies of tormented souls, these creatures have adopted ghostlike abilities that make them quite elusive.', -1, 0),
(401586, 15, 5, 'Armored Golden Pterrordax', 401586, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401586, 6, 1, 'Painted and adorned with gold, these Pterrordax patrol the skies over the tomb of Atal\'Dazar.', -1, 0),
(401587, 15, 5, 'Zereth Overseer', 401587, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401587, 6, 1, 'Enigmatic and aloof, this construct of the First Ones flies on a graceful stream of perfect geometric understanding.', -1, 0),
(401588, 15, 5, 'Winding Slitherdrake', 401588, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401588, 6, 1, 'These drakes feel at home in the depths of the earth and the far reaches of the sky.', -1, 0),
(401589, 15, 5, 'Renewed Proto-Drake', 401589, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401589, 6, 1, 'As the isles awaken, these proto-drakes answer the call to soar the skies alongside mortals.', -1, 0),
(401590, 15, 5, 'Windborne Velocidrake', 401590, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401590, 6, 1, 'The long talons of the velocidrake give it an edge on the plains.', -1, 0),
(401591, 15, 5, 'Cliffside Wylderdrake', 401591, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401591, 6, 1, 'Often roosting along the steep cliff faces of Thaldraszus, they\'re swift to the skies in times of danger.', -1, 0),
(401594, 15, 5, 'Jade, Bright Foreseer', 401594, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401594, 6, 1, 'The presence of this majestic Pandaren rabbit spirit brings joy and happiness and is heralded as a wonderful omen. Legend says that in its eyes, you can glimpse the greatest happiness of your life, even if it is yet to come.', -1, 0),
(401595, 15, 5, 'Cerulean Marsh Hopper', 401595, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401595, 6, 1, 'Gottum\'s expansion into export markets was inevitable with news of the Trading Post reaching even into the depths of the Frogmarsh.', -1, 0),
(401596, 15, 5, 'Amalgam of Rage', 401596, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401596, 6, 1, 'The fearsome beast ridden by Astaroth himself is now yours to command.', -1, 0),
(401597, 15, 5, 'Grimhowl', 401597, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401597, 6, 1, 'Otherwise known as The Flame Woof, the Fetcher of the Igneous, Molten Core\'s Best Friend, Forgehound Maximus, the Best Fiery Boy, and "oh no is that an AXE on his face!?"', -1, 0),
(401599, 15, 5, 'Eternal Gladiator\'s Soul Eater', 401599, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401599, 6, 1, 'This soul eater\'s gaze unnerves you. Best not meet its eyes for too long.', -1, 0),
(401600, 15, 5, 'Elusive Emerald Hawkstrider', 401600, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401600, 6, 1, 'Unseen for many years, this brightly hued hawkstrider emerged from hiding to help defend the Ghostlands from the Scourge. Its prowess shines as brilliantly as its feathers.', -1, 0),
(401602, 15, 5, 'Tuskarr Shoreglider', 401602, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401602, 6, 1, 'The Tuskarr learned long ago that some of the bones of the sea creatures they hunted were light and buoyant, making for effective glider materials.', -1, 0),
(401603, 15, 5, 'Subterranean Magmammoth', 401603, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401603, 6, 1, 'Awakened from a long slumber, this beast has yet to see the light of day.', -1, 0),
(401612, 15, 5, 'Loyal Magmammoth', 401612, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401612, 6, 1, 'Liberated from the Qalashi and harnessed by your ingenuity (and your harness), this magmammoth is ready to lava stomp wherever you want to go.', -1, 0),
(401614, 15, 5, 'Stormtouched Bruffalon', 401614, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401614, 6, 1, 'Even from within her prison, Raszageth\'s primal scorn brought the mightiest beasts to heel.', -1, 0),
(401615, 15, 5, 'Tamed Skitterfly', 401615, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401615, 6, 1, 'It didn\'t take long for Granpap Whiskers to tame the skitterflies around the Dragonscale Basecamp and set them to helping move Expedition personnel and cargo.', -1, 0),
(401616, 15, 5, 'Azure Skitterfly', 401616, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401616, 6, 1, 'Once Granpap Whiskers finally taught them how to take riders, the azure skitterflies proved to bond closely and loyally to their riders.', -1, 0),
(401617, 15, 5, 'Verdant Skitterfly', 401617, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401617, 6, 1, 'Verdant skitterflies are the perfect mount for the scouts of the Dragonscale Expedition scouts, as they are fast and blend into the foliage of the Dragon Isles.', -1, 0),
(401618, 15, 5, 'Bestowed Sandskimmer', 401618, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401618, 6, 1, 'A gift from Granpap Whiskers, these capricious skitterflies help the Timewalkers clean up present (and future) sand-related temporal calamities.', -1, 0),
(401619, 15, 5, 'Ancient Salamanther', 401619, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401619, 6, 1, 'Due to their preference for dark caves and murky waters, sightings of this unique breed of salamanther are so rare that many researchers thought they had gone extinct.', -1, 0),
(401621, 15, 5, 'Coralscale Salamanther', 401621, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401621, 6, 1, 'As Raszageth\'s storms abated, this aquatic breed of salamanther was among the many wonders to settle among the shores in their wake.', -1, 0),
(401622, 15, 5, 'Stormhide Salamanther', 401622, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401622, 6, 1, 'Sometimes when storm energies infuse a creature, it simply... becomes larger and more placid. Few salamanthers are willing to be ridden, but these children of the storm are a notable exception.', -1, 0),
(401623, 15, 5, 'Seething Slug', 401623, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401623, 6, 1, 'Drawn forth from its abyss by the rage of the Zaqali.', -1, 0),
(401626, 15, 5, 'Shellack', 401626, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401626, 6, 1, 'Fed by victory and hardened by glory, this snail is nothing less than a tribute to mastery.', -1, 0),
(401627, 15, 5, 'Gooey Snailemental', 401627, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401627, 6, 1, 'Formed from the leftover elemental energies of the Primal Storms, this magical mollusk is faster than it appears.', -1, 0),
(401629, 15, 5, 'Scrappy Worldsnail', 401629, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401629, 6, 1, 'For the Worldbreakers, a portable footstool. For you, a hardy mount.', -1, 0),
(401633, 15, 5, 'Bestowed Trawling Mammoth', 401633, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401633, 6, 1, 'A gift from Scout Tomul, so that the feasts of Iskaara will always have enough fish to feed those in need.', -1, 0),
(401634, 15, 5, 'Mossy Mammoth', 401634, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401634, 6, 1, 'Preserved for thousands of years in stone, bronze magic has nearly aged this mammoth back into a fossil.', -1, 0),
(401635, 15, 5, 'Plainswalker Bearer', 401635, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401635, 6, 1, 'The mammoths of the Ohn\'ahran Plains are unaccustomed to carrying people, as their centaur neighbors do not typically ride mounts. They can learn to bear riders, however. Some even do so enthusiastically.', -1, 0),
(401638, 15, 5, 'Explorer\'s Stonehide Packbeast', 401638, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401638, 6, 1, 'A true explorer never stays in one place for long. Having a reliable packbeast with a strong back and sturdy legs is essential for travel.', -1, 0),
(401639, 15, 5, 'Lizi, Thunderspine Tramper', 401639, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401639, 6, 1, 'Nothing will stop Lizi from her mission to eat all the world\'s fruit.', -1, 0),
(401644, 15, 5, 'Raging Magmammoth', 401644, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401644, 6, 1, 'Most lava flows. This lava charges.', -1, 0),
(401645, 15, 5, 'Renewed Magmammoth', 401645, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401645, 6, 1, 'Reforged after destruction at the hands of the Druids of the Flame, this magmammoth is ready to stomp any foes in its path.', -1, 0),
(401651, 15, 5, 'Bestowed Ottuk Vanguard', 401651, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401651, 6, 1, 'A gift from Brena, the Iskaara sent their most loyal (and adorable) companions to watch over Kalecgos and his reuinited family in Valdrakken', -1, 0),
(401653, 15, 5, 'Brown War Ottuk', 401653, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401653, 6, 1, 'The tuskarr of Iskaara are loathe to war against anyone, but many tuskarr and their allies have nonetheless taken up the spear with a war ottuk beside them.', -1, 0),
(401654, 15, 5, 'Otterworldly Ottuk Carrier', 401654, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401654, 6, 1, 'Some ottuks get into the spirit of carrying people around more than others.', -1, 0),
(401655, 15, 5, 'Yellow War Ottuk', 401655, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401655, 6, 1, 'The yellow ottuks of the Azure Span are sleek, sneaky, and smart. Those trained for war are the finest tuskarr cavalry mounts, equally capable on the ground and in the waters.', -1, 0),
(401656, 15, 5, 'Otto', 401656, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401656, 6, 1, 'Relax. The future will unfold as it was meant to, one way or an otter.', -1, 0),
(401657, 15, 5, 'Brown Scouting Ottuk', 401657, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401657, 6, 1, 'Wily and playful in their natural habitat, ottuks possess keen eyes that can scout far afield as ably as they watch for predators.', -1, 0),
(401658, 15, 5, 'Ivory Trader\'s Ottuk', 401658, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401658, 6, 1, 'No adult knows why some ottuks are white, but any tuskarr child can tell you: it\'s because they eat too much snow.', -1, 0),
(401659, 15, 5, 'Yellow Scouting Ottuk', 401659, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401659, 6, 1, 'The yellow scouting ottuk love to hide and they blend in well to their surroundings. When not \'playing\' hide and seek with their riders, they are perfect companions when scouting enemy encampments.', -1, 0),
(401660, 15, 5, 'Crimson Gladiator\'s Drake', 401660, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401660, 6, 1, 'Forged in the fires of conquest, and armored to the teeth.', -1, 0),
(401662, 15, 5, 'Telix the Stormhorn', 401662, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401662, 6, 1, 'Once a simple beetle of the Forbidden Reach, Telix became infused with storm magic when Raszageth was unleashed. With its newly heightened senses, Telix roams the Dragon Isles alongside the Dragonscale Expedition--and you!', -1, 0),
(401664, 15, 5, 'Guardian Vorquin', 401664, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401664, 6, 1, 'Trained using ancient dracthyr methods, these armored vorquin are the pinnacle of tactical mounted ground warfare.', -1, 0),
(401665, 15, 5, 'Swift Armored Vorquin', 401665, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401665, 6, 1, 'Trained using ancient dracthyr methods, these armored vorquin are the pinnacle of tactical mounted ground warfare.', -1, 0),
(401667, 15, 5, 'Armored Vorquin Leystrider', 401667, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401667, 6, 1, 'Trained using ancient dracthyr methods, these armored vorquin are the pinnacle of tactical mounted ground warfare.', -1, 0),
(401668, 15, 5, 'Majestic Armored Vorquin', 401668, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401668, 6, 1, 'Trained using ancient dracthyr methods, these armored vorquin are the pinnacle of tactical mounted ground warfare.', -1, 0),
(401669, 15, 5, 'Bestowed Ohuna Spotter', 401669, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401669, 6, 1, 'A gift from the Ohn\'ir, these ohuna are invaluable companions when scouting new horizons for the Dragonscale Expedition.', -1, 0),
(401671, 15, 5, 'Duskwing Ohuna', 401671, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401671, 6, 1, 'If you look to the night sky and see the clouds whisk by don\'t panic. It may just be the illusive Duskwing Ohuna.', -1, 0),
(401672, 15, 5, 'Zenet Hatchling', 401672, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401672, 6, 1, 'The hardest winds begin with a gust and a flap.', -1, 0),
(401674, 15, 5, 'Temperamental Skyclaw', 401674, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401674, 6, 1, 'Slyverns are rarely comfortable acting as mounts. Only those willing to feed their gluttonous appetites and keep a careful eye on them should attempt to ride.', -1, 0),
(401679, 15, 5, 'Frostbrood Proto-Wyrm', 401679, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401679, 6, 1, 'The same magic of undeath that raised the Frostbrood into the Lich King\'s service has infused this primal wyrm. Its loyalty and ferocity now serve those who defend Azeroth.', -1, 0),
(401681, 15, 5, 'Hailstorm Armoredon', 401681, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401681, 6, 1, 'Born in the middle of an ice storm, this armoredon prefers its meals partially frozen.', -1, 0),
(401683, 15, 5, 'Crimson Vorquin', 401683, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401683, 6, 1, 'Respected for their resilience in battle, even against dragonfire, these noble beasts are the prized mounts of the dracthyr cavalry.', -1, 0),
(401684, 15, 5, 'Sapphire Vorquin', 401684, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401684, 6, 1, 'Respected for their resilience in battle, even against dragonfire, these noble beasts are the prized mounts of the dracthyr cavalry.', -1, 0),
(401685, 15, 5, 'Bronze Vorquin', 401685, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401685, 6, 1, 'Respected for their resilience in battle, even against dragonfire, these noble beasts are the prized mounts of the dracthyr cavalry.', -1, 0),
(401686, 15, 5, 'Obsidian Vorquin', 401686, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401686, 6, 1, 'Respected for their resilience in battle, even against dragonfire, these noble beasts are the prized mounts of the dracthyr cavalry.', -1, 0),
(401688, 15, 5, 'Vicious Sabertooth', 401688, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401688, 6, 1, 'The elite Alliance forces that use these sabertooth mounts use a battle cry that translates from Darnassian as "here kitty kitty".', -1, 0),
(401689, 15, 5, 'Vicious Sabertooth', 401689, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401689, 6, 1, 'The elite Horde forces that use these sabertooth mounts use a battle cry that translates from Thalassian as "pspspspsps".', -1, 0),
(401690, 15, 5, 'Whelpling', 401690, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401690, 6, 1, '', -1, 0),
(401692, 15, 5, 'Wondrous Wavewhisker', 401692, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401692, 6, 1, 'They say one of these magical fish is born when a fisherfolk dreams of the one that got away... and grows bigger with each retelling of the tale.', -1, 0),
(401698, 15, 5, 'Rocket Shredder 9001', 401698, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401698, 6, 1, 'The salesgoblin always tells people about the RS-9001\'s huge variety of attachments, but somehow neglects to mention that you never get to pick the attachments it\'ll have when you mount up.', -1, 0),
(401699, 15, 5, 'Gleaming Moonbeast', 401699, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401699, 6, 1, 'Armored in glistening silver, these devoted mounts are said to be a blessing from Elune herself.', -1, 0),
(401710, 15, 5, 'Black-Furred Bakar', 401710, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401710, 6, 1, 'Such a good boy. Or girl. It\'s hard to tell sometimes. Always good though.', -1, 0),
(401725, 15, 5, 'Inferno Armoredon', 401725, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401725, 6, 1, 'Its tail smells like campfire but its breath smells like brimstone.', -1, 0),
(401729, 15, 5, 'Big Slick in the City', 401729, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401729, 6, 1, 'Big heart, big dreams, Big Slick.', -1, 0),
(401730, 15, 5, 'Igneous Shalewing', 401730, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401730, 6, 1, 'You\'d be forgiven for mistaking this creature for a flying volcanic rock. Because to some extent, it is.', -1, 0),
(401732, 15, 5, 'Cobalt Shalewing', 401732, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401732, 6, 1, 'Brood of Karokta, raised in the underlight of Zaralek Cavern.', -1, 0),
(401733, 15, 5, 'Calescent Shalewing', 401733, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401733, 6, 1, 'A shalewing born in the wake of Fyrakk\'s destructive breach. Cursed by his primal flame, its temperature slowly but constantly rises. It must immerse itself in water to cool off periodically, lest its own heat smother it.', -1, 0),
(401734, 15, 5, 'Shadowflame Shalewing', 401734, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401734, 6, 1, 'Born from the magma, its carapace was originally molten blobs cooled to form dark-colored volcanic rock. Being imbued by shadowflame has only solidified its unbreakable nature.', -1, 0),
(401735, 15, 5, 'Cataloged Shalewing', 401735, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401735, 6, 1, 'The first instance of a flaming shalewing ever discovered. Nine out of ten researchers agree: it\'s hot!', -1, 0),
(401736, 15, 5, 'Boulder Hauler', 401736, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401736, 6, 1, 'These shalewings have been specially trained to carry large amounts of Barter Boulders for the niffen\'s bartering activities.', -1, 0),
(401737, 15, 5, 'Sandy Shalewing', 401737, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401737, 6, 1, 'The patterns on the wings of that creature resemble sand flowing through an hourglass. One could gaze upon them for ages...', -1, 0),
(401738, 15, 5, 'Morsel Sniffer', 401738, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401738, 6, 1, 'A breed of shalewings trained by the niffen to find the deepest of morsels.', -1, 0),
(401739, 15, 5, 'Obsidian Gladiator\'s Slitherdrake', 401739, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401739, 6, 1, 'This mischievous drake enjoys flying through geysers and volcanic plumes.', -1, 0),
(401740, 15, 5, 'Vicious War Snail', 401740, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401740, 6, 1, 'The Alliance uses these ravenous snail mounts to traverse over any obstacle in battlefields.', -1, 0),
(401741, 15, 5, 'Vicious War Snail', 401741, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401741, 6, 1, 'The Horde uses these ravenous snail mounts to traverse over any obstacle in battlefields.', -1, 0),
(401742, 15, 5, 'Felcrystal Scorpion', 401742, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401742, 6, 1, 'The results of a fel infusion experiment with one of Skorpyron\'s offspring.', -1, 0),
(401744, 15, 5, 'Grotto Netherwing Drake', 401744, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401744, 6, 1, 'After traveling to Outland and back, it\'s only natural these drakes seek out new skies.', -1, 0),
(401772, 15, 5, 'Scarlet Pterrordax', 401772, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401772, 6, 1, 'This pterrordax was so eager to take to the skies that its handler couldn\'t finish training it.', -1, 0),
(401773, 15, 5, 'Harbor Gryphon', 401773, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401773, 6, 1, 'This gryphon was the runt of its pride, left behind when its brethren were sent for training. Today, however, it is ready to prove its worth.', -1, 0),
(401774, 15, 5, 'Valiance', 401774, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401774, 6, 1, 'Most undead steeds have their riders chosen for them. Valiance, on the other hand, chooses its own rider.', -1, 0),
(401776, 15, 5, 'White War Wolf', 401776, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401776, 6, 1, 'Can a wolf\'s hunger ever be satiated? These lupine brutes seek and devour the enemies of the Horde.', -1, 0),
(401777, 15, 5, 'Ravenous Black Gryphon', 401777, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401777, 6, 1, 'War corrupted these once-proud creatures. The susurration of their wings now whispers omens of imminent demise.', -1, 0),
(401778, 15, 5, 'Gold-Toed Albatross', 401778, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401778, 6, 1, 'Soaring from a distant timeway, this never-before-seen avian variant was born in a world of order.', -1, 0),
(401779, 15, 5, 'Felstorm Dragon', 401779, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401779, 6, 1, 'The Burning Legion defeated dragons in a distant timeway. These foul fel wyrms chose corruption and servitude over destruction.', -1, 0),
(401781, 15, 5, 'Sulfur Hound', 401781, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401781, 6, 1, 'The Black Empire subjugated these humbled and hateful hounds. Utterly obedient, they still serve the strong.', -1, 0),
(401782, 15, 5, 'Perfected Juggernaut', 401782, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401782, 6, 1, 'Perfection, like beauty, is in the eye of the beholder. But eyesight can be surgically enhanced.', -1, 0),
(401783, 15, 5, 'Scourgebound Vanquisher', 401783, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401783, 6, 1, 'Once bound in service to the Scourge, these undead dragons exist only to spread death, disease, and destruction.', -1, 0),
(401784, 15, 5, 'Royal Swarmer', 401784, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401784, 6, 1, 'These drones will swarm anyone who dares approach their queen uninvited.', -1, 0),
(401785, 15, 5, 'Ancestral Clefthoof', 401785, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401785, 6, 1, 'This clefthoof has seen ages pass, witnessing everything and patiently teaching many to ride.', -1, 0),
(401792, 15, 5, 'Algarian Stormrider', 401792, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401792, 6, 1, 'Flying true even in the harshest conditions, this lightning-infused rook was trained to soar through the skies of the Isle of Dorn and into the depths below.', -1, 0),
(401794, 15, 5, 'Pattie', 401794, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401794, 6, 1, 'Preservationist Kathos encountered Pattie on her first assignment to Vol\'dun. Pattie developed an affinity to Preservationist work but is eager to delve deeper, helping adventurers in their sleuthing.', -1, 0),
(401795, 15, 5, 'Auspicious Arborwyrm', 401795, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401795, 6, 1, 'Sprouting to life only once every sixty years, this living wooden dragon combines the patience of a tree and the grace of a dragon in flight.', -1, 0),
(401796, 15, 5, 'Whelpling', 401796, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401796, 6, 1, '', -1, 0),
(401797, 15, 5, 'Ginormous Grrloc', 401797, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401797, 6, 1, 'It\'s the second biggest murloc you\'ve ever seen!', -1, 0),
(401798, 15, 5, 'Azure Worldchiller', 401798, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401798, 6, 1, 'In the corners of Azeroth, stories are told of a dreaded dragon who swept a pall of torment over the land. In some versions of this story, his fiery presence brought cataclysmic death and destruction worldwide. In other versions, he is blue.', -1, 0),
(401799, 15, 5, 'Eve\'s Ghastly Rider', 401799, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401799, 6, 1, 'The preferred transportation of the Fenlow family (especially during Hallow\'s End).', -1, 0),
(401801, 15, 5, 'Verdant Armoredon', 401801, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401801, 6, 1, 'The gnarled horns of this armoredon are far stronger than bone.', -1, 0),
(401808, 15, 5, 'Blossoming Dreamstag', 401808, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401808, 6, 1, 'The pelts of young dreamstags flower with the vibrant colors of the dream.', -1, 0),
(401809, 15, 5, 'Suntouched Dreamstag', 401809, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401809, 6, 1, 'The sun\'s radiant energy nurtures these dreamstags, helping them rapidly reach maturity.', -1, 0),
(401810, 15, 5, 'Rekindled Dreamstag', 401810, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401810, 6, 1, 'Ashes of fallen leaves are fertile soil for dreamstags to arise from.', -1, 0),
(401811, 15, 5, 'Lunar Dreamstag', 401811, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401811, 6, 1, 'The moon\'s pale light is reflected in the pelt of these elusive nocturnal creatures.', -1, 0),
(401812, 15, 5, 'Runebound Firelord', 401812, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401812, 6, 1, 'By fire be purged the obstacles in your path!', -1, 0),
(401813, 15, 5, 'Mimiron\'s Jumpjets', 401813, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401813, 6, 1, 'Created as a prototype by Mimiron. The pieces were stolen from his workshop, sold, and lost to time. That is until now..', -1, 0),
(401814, 15, 5, 'Shadow Dusk Dreamsaber', 401814, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401814, 6, 1, 'A dreamsaber strikes quickly from the shadows, capturing small animals and slipping back into darkness without a sound. The lucky few who have seen a feeding dreamsaber can see them revel in lazily toying with their prey before beginning their meal.', -1, 0),
(401815, 15, 5, 'Winter Night Dreamsaber', 401815, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401815, 6, 1, 'These nocturnal dreamsabers carry the chill of winter with them and will often hibernate for days on end if not otherwise awoken.', -1, 0),
(401816, 15, 5, 'Evening Sun Dreamsaber', 401816, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401816, 6, 1, 'These dreamsabers are ferocious in battle, yet lethargic and often found lazily outstretched upon open fields. After soaking in the warmth of daylight, their flame flares that much brighter.', -1, 0),
(401817, 15, 5, 'Morning Flourish Dreamsaber', 401817, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401817, 6, 1, 'Known for the lavish energy that emanates from them, these sabers are notorious tricksters. Their roar scatters the early birds that wake them.', -1, 0),
(401818, 15, 5, 'Anu\'relos, Flame\'s Guidance', 401818, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401818, 6, 1, 'Though her feathers flicker with flame\'s destructive potential, they do not scorch, but simply radiate a comfortable heat.', -1, 0),
(401819, 15, 5, 'Vicious Moonbeast', 401819, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401819, 6, 1, 'Unlike most of its kind, this moonbeast has a taste for Horde blood and an affinity for the color blue.', -1, 0),
(401820, 15, 5, 'Vicious Moonbeast', 401820, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401820, 6, 1, 'Unlike most of its kind, this moonbeast has a taste for Alliance blood and an affinity for the color red.', -1, 0),
(401822, 15, 5, 'Draconic Gladiator\'s Drake', 401822, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401822, 6, 1, 'Its wings darken the skies with the shadow of conquest.', -1, 0),
(401824, 15, 5, 'Brown-Furred Spiky Bakar', 401824, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401824, 6, 1, 'Such a good boy. Or girl. It\'s hard to tell sometimes. Always good though.', -1, 0),
(401825, 15, 5, 'Taivan', 401825, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401825, 6, 1, 'You don\'t have to be what the world expects you to be. Be who Taivan knows you *can* be.', -1, 0),
(401830, 15, 5, 'Flourishing Whimsydrake', 401830, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401830, 6, 1, 'These playful protectors of the Emerald Dream may be larger than their faerie dragon relatives, but they are no less mischievous.', -1, 0),
(401831, 15, 5, 'Verdant Gladiator\'s Slitherdrake', 401831, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401831, 6, 1, 'This drake visited many heroes in their dreams before joining your cause.', -1, 0),
(401833, 15, 5, 'Springtide Dreamtalon', 401833, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401833, 6, 1, 'Surging with the kind of energy and enthusiasm that can make anyone envious.', -1, 0),
(401834, 15, 5, 'Ochre Dreamtalon', 401834, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401834, 6, 1, 'Playful dreamtalons often decorate themselves in a myriad of colors that only autumn offers.', -1, 0),
(401835, 15, 5, 'Snowfluff Dreamtalon', 401835, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401835, 6, 1, 'As lighthearted and gentle as the snow, they can bounce from one snowdrift to the next without leaving a print.', -1, 0),
(401837, 15, 5, 'Delugen', 401837, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401837, 6, 1, 'Imagine being so engrossed by a dream that it feels real; some might even call it a delusion.', -1, 0),
(401838, 15, 5, 'Talont', 401838, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401838, 6, 1, 'Some daydreams are filled with wondrous possibilities, but shatter when reminded of reality\'s limitations. Some dreams are not so burdened, even when they carry a rider.', -1, 0),
(401839, 15, 5, 'Stargrazer', 401839, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401839, 6, 1, 'One can\'t help but think what it might feel like to pluck the stars from their fixture in the sky. Perhaps, Stargrazer will show us how someday.', -1, 0),
(401841, 15, 5, 'Crimson Glimmerfur', 401841, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401841, 6, 1, 'Gilnean legend states this red-and-white fox only crosses the Winter Veil during one season.', -1, 0),
(401938, 15, 5, 'Mammyth', 401938, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401938, 6, 1, 'In the Dream, sometimes the myth is more real than its basis.', -1, 0),
(401939, 15, 5, 'Imagiwing', 401939, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401939, 6, 1, 'There\'s nothing more beautiful than watching your imagination take flight.', -1, 0),
(401940, 15, 5, 'Salatrancer', 401940, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401940, 6, 1, 'While most salamanthers\' attention jumps freely from one attraction to the next, this one enjoys long periods of deep observation.', -1, 0),
(401941, 15, 5, 'Heartseeker Mana Ray', 401941, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401941, 6, 1, 'Someone once told this mana ray it was adorable. It has been pursuing that positive feeling ever since.', -1, 0),
(401942, 15, 5, 'Jeweled Copper Scarab', 401942, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401942, 6, 1, 'The rulers of desert kingdoms would attune crystals to their personal mounts for quick summoning.', -1, 0),
(401943, 15, 5, 'Incognitro, the Indecipherable Felcycle', 401943, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401943, 6, 1, 'This demonic machine was designed by Chief Engineer Ulzik as an experiment in cross-dimensional traversal. Despite many deaths during testing, Ulzik remained confident that this vehicle would reveal secrets of the universe previously unknowable.', -1, 0),
(401944, 15, 5, 'Golden Regal Scarab', 401944, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401944, 6, 1, 'Plated with gold and socketed with emeralds, this scarab is fit to fly royalty in style.', -1, 0),
(401945, 15, 5, 'Jeweled Sapphire Scarab', 401945, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401945, 6, 1, 'Begifted to a young Tol\'vir Princess, this ornate jeweled statue was brought to life by the Gemseers of Ramkahen.', -1, 0),
(401946, 15, 5, 'Jeweled Jade Scarab', 401946, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401946, 6, 1, 'The razor-thin wings of this scarab are well-protected by a gleaming, yet indestructible jade-carved carapace.', -1, 0),
(401947, 15, 5, 'Hateforged Blazecycle', 401947, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401947, 6, 1, 'This sweet deathcycle lets you go on your very own burning rubber crusade!', -1, 0),
(401948, 15, 5, 'Voidfire Deathcycle', 401948, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401948, 6, 1, 'The prized possession of Haymar the devout. Unclear if he would be anything if not for his epic void bike. Formerly assigned to patrolling the streets of Stormwind after its fall.', -1, 0),
(401949, 15, 5, 'Gilnean Prowler', 401949, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401949, 6, 1, 'A scrupulous breed of prowlers whose ferocity can only be matched by that of the worgen. These decisive creatures embody discipline and a controlled viciousness that even the worgen have come to admire.', -1, 0),
(401956, 15, 5, 'Fur-endship Fox', 401956, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401956, 6, 1, 'These magical creatures thrive on love and friendship.', -1, 0),
(401957, 15, 5, 'Soaring Sky Fox', 401957, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401957, 6, 1, 'Take to the sky on the most loyal and loving fox on Azeroth.', -1, 0),
(401958, 15, 5, 'Twilight Sky Prowler', 401958, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401958, 6, 1, 'Dubbed the midnight trickster by some, many a couple point to him as the reason their paths crossed in the night.', -1, 0),
(401959, 15, 5, 'Compass Rose', 401959, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 401959, 6, 1, 'Pried from a giant Hearthstone game box.', -1, 0),
(402023, 15, 5, 'Noble Flying Carpet', 402023, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402023, 6, 1, 'Mages celebrating Noblegarden turned their ordinary festive decor into floating spectacles, only to have them stolen by an angry druid.', -1, 0),
(402035, 15, 5, 'Majestic Azure Peafowl', 402035, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402035, 6, 1, 'The peafowl is renowned for its stunning colors and plumage.', -1, 0),
(402036, 15, 5, 'Brilliant Sunburst Peafowl', 402036, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402036, 6, 1, 'With this bird, feathers will never be out of style.', -1, 0),
(402038, 15, 5, 'Clayscale Hornstrider', 402038, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402038, 6, 1, 'Named for their dusty-red appearance, clayscale hornstriders can be found tearing across the muddy hills of the Ohn\'ahran Plains.', -1, 0),
(402039, 15, 5, 'Savage Blue Battle Turtle', 402039, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402039, 6, 1, 'Don\'t feel blue chasing your foes, you\'ve got cannons. Nothing can outrun a cannon.', -1, 0),
(402055, 15, 5, 'Infinite Armoredon', 402055, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402055, 6, 1, 'Even among the armoredon, the possibilities for the future are infinite.', -1, 0),
(402056, 15, 5, 'Vicious Dreamtalon', 402056, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402056, 6, 1, 'This feline beast\'s preferred prey is the Horde.', -1, 0),
(402057, 15, 5, 'Vicious Dreamtalon', 402057, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402057, 6, 1, 'This feline beast\'s preferred prey is the Alliance.', -1, 0),
(402060, 15, 5, 'Golden Discus', 402060, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402060, 6, 1, 'An ancient mogu artifact awarded to those who are deeply committed to forms of currency.', -1, 0),
(402063, 15, 5, 'Mogu Hazeblazer', 402063, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402063, 6, 1, 'This ancient mogu artifact controls ambient fog to enable levitation.', -1, 0),
(402064, 15, 5, 'Sky Surfer', 402064, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402064, 6, 1, 'An ancient mogu artifact awarded to those who are deeply committed to the skies.', -1, 0),
(402065, 15, 5, 'Daystorm Windsteed', 402065, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402065, 6, 1, 'It is said that when lightning strikes the sun, a gleaming beast in red armor would emerge from the heavens. The Daystorm Windsteed has never heard of these legends and has been here the entire time.', -1, 0),
(402067, 15, 5, 'Forest Windsteed', 402067, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402067, 6, 1, 'The fur of this Windsteed is not only colored to match its woodland home, but also usually contains bits of bark and leaves.', -1, 0),
(402068, 15, 5, 'Dashing Windsteed', 402068, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402068, 6, 1, 'Windsteeds are incredibly gentle and easy to train... if you can catch one.', -1, 0),
(402069, 15, 5, 'Feathered Windsurfer', 402069, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402069, 6, 1, 'Check the current windspeed and elevation before mounting. Avoid trees and other tall objects. Damaged kites are ineligible for return or refund. - Windsurfer\'s Instruction Manual', -1, 0),
(402070, 15, 5, 'Guardian Quilen', 402070, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402070, 6, 1, 'When Quan the Relentless fell in battle, his loyal hounds waited for his return. Millenia later, they remain patient.', -1, 0),
(402071, 15, 5, 'Marble Quilen', 402071, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402071, 6, 1, 'Created by a mogu sorcerer who breathed life into their favorite pet rock.', -1, 0),
(402072, 15, 5, 'Gilded Riding Crane', 402072, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402072, 6, 1, 'It is said that an emperor once paid a large sum for a golden crane. Upon discovering that the crane was only colored like that of the precious metal, he hid with shame in his bedchambers for a week.', -1, 0),
(402073, 15, 5, 'Pale Riding Crane', 402073, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402073, 6, 1, 'I looked, and behold, a pale... crane?', -1, 0),
(402074, 15, 5, 'Rose Riding Crane', 402074, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402074, 6, 1, 'This brightly-colored bird is often confused with a flamingo or marabou.', -1, 0),
(402075, 15, 5, 'Silver Riding Crane', 402075, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402075, 6, 1, 'This tall bird is one of the most graceful and elegant cranes, slightly moreso than the Bronze Crane but less than the Golden Crane.', -1, 0),
(402076, 15, 5, 'Luxurious Riding Crane', 402076, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402076, 6, 1, 'A majestic bird, but a rather picky eater.', -1, 0),
(402077, 15, 5, 'Tropical Riding Crane', 402077, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402077, 6, 1, 'This Jade Forest native uses its coloration as camouflage.', -1, 0),
(402078, 15, 5, 'Snowy Riding Goat', 402078, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402078, 6, 1, 'The Kun-Lai Summit mountain goats are known for climbing even the highest peaks in search of kafa beans and salt licks.', -1, 0),
(402080, 15, 5, 'Little Red Riding Goat', 402080, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402080, 6, 1, 'What this goat lacks in size, it makes up for in stubbornness.', -1, 0),
(402081, 15, 5, 'Bloody Skyscreamer', 402081, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402081, 6, 1, 'This dinosaur still harbors the rage of its ancestors from the Zandalari Invasion.', -1, 0),
(402083, 15, 5, 'Night Pterrorwing', 402083, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402083, 6, 1, 'Scholars interpret this creature\'s awful screeching as "fear me, I am the night!"', -1, 0),
(402084, 15, 5, 'Jade Pterrordax', 402084, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402084, 6, 1, 'This favored mount of the Zandalari is a great singer, or so it thinks.', -1, 0),
(402085, 15, 5, 'Cobalt Juggernaut', 402085, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402085, 6, 1, 'What started as a rideable mining and logging machine devolved quickly into chaos when engineers asked themselves if they could make it any cooler.', -1, 0),
(402086, 15, 5, 'Fel Iron Juggernaut', 402086, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402086, 6, 1, 'This war machine was stolen from a timeline in which Garrosh Hellscream joined the Burning Legion. Suffice it to say, there is not much left of that timeline.', -1, 0),
(402087, 15, 5, 'Purple Shado-Pan Riding Tiger', 402087, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402087, 6, 1, 'When waking a tiger, use a long stick. Better yet, tell your friend to wake the tiger instead. -Pandaren Proverb', -1, 0),
(402088, 15, 5, 'Riverwalker Mushan', 402088, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402088, 6, 1, 'The Mushan is a voracious beast. Though it can be tamed, it will demand a second, third, and even fourth breakfast every day.', -1, 0),
(402089, 15, 5, 'Palehide Mushan Beast', 402089, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402089, 6, 1, 'The Palehide Mushan is the tastiest of Mushan beasts, but it hates being reminded of that fact.', -1, 0),
(402090, 15, 5, 'Polly Roger', 402090, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402090, 6, 1, 'The scourge of the slightly-northeastern seas, giant parrots like Polly can live for up to 2000 years. What a wonderful curse on your next of kin.', -1, 0),
(402091, 15, 5, 'Voyaging Wilderling', 402091, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402091, 6, 1, 'These playful visitors from another realm thrive while traveling to new lands with new friends.', -1, 0),
(402114, 15, 5, 'Zovaal\'s Soul Eater', 402114, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402114, 6, 1, 'Was I a good boy? the soul asked Zovaal. "No. I\'m told you were the worst."', -1, 0),
(402116, 15, 5, 'Remembered Golden Gryphon', 402116, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402116, 6, 1, 'They love lions in Stormwind, and the gryphon is half lion. This is why these creatures are an air travel staple throughout the Alliance.', -1, 0),
(402117, 15, 5, 'Remembered Wind Rider', 402117, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402117, 6, 1, 'Hundreds of battles across a dozen campaigns have been fought and won on the backs of these honored creatures.', -1, 0),
(402118, 15, 5, 'Amber Pterrordax', 402118, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402118, 6, 1, 'The Pterrordax could and would eat you in seconds. Are you sure sitting on its back is a good idea?', -1, 0),
(402119, 15, 5, 'Stonevault Mechsuit', 402119, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402119, 6, 1, 'Metal once ruined, restored to life by scrap and song.', -1, 0),
(402140, 15, 5, 'Charming Courier', 402140, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402140, 6, 1, 'Neither snow nor rain nor heat nor gloom of night stays these charming couriers from the swift completion of their appointed rounds.', -1, 0),
(402142, 15, 5, 'August Phoenix', 402142, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402142, 6, 1, 'The magnificent August Phoenixes are blessed by Chi-Ji to fill the hearts of riders with wonder and hope for the future.', -1, 0),
(402143, 15, 5, 'Astral Emperor\'s Serpent', 402143, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402143, 6, 1, 'After the unburdened Emperor Shaohao gave his final breath to protect his people, a golden serpent descended from the heavens to alight the emperor\'s spirit to the peaks of Kun-Lai Summit.', -1, 0),
(402144, 15, 5, 'Delver\'s Dirigible', 402144, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402144, 6, 1, 'This aircraft will help you delve straight into adventure, wherever it may be!', -1, 0),
(402145, 15, 5, 'Kickin\' Kezan Waveshredder', 402145, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402145, 6, 1, 'If everybody had an ocean, they\'d go surfing with this sweet waveshredder. But in the case of not having an ocean, you can surf the skies! Hang 8!', -1, 0),
(402148, 15, 5, 'Smoldering Cinderbee', 402148, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402148, 6, 1, 'A somewhat surprising choice of mount, the Council of Dornogal assures you riding it is safe. Mostly.', -1, 0),
(402150, 15, 5, 'Vicious Skyflayer', 402150, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402150, 6, 1, 'This creature hungers for battle with the contemptible Alliance.', -1, 0),
(402152, 15, 5, 'Pearlescent Goblin Wave Shredder', 402152, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402152, 6, 1, 'Surf the shores of Stranglethorn in style!', -1, 0),
(402158, 15, 5, 'Crowd Pummeler 2-30', 402158, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402158, 6, 1, 'Guaranteed to knock the teeth out from your enemies with a single punch!', -1, 0),
(402159, 15, 5, 'Machine Defense Unit 1-11', 402159, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402159, 6, 1, 'One of many such mechsuits designed to guard the Machine. After years of faithful service it is no longer suited for combat. It does make for an impressive conveyance, though.', -1, 0),
(402161, 15, 5, 'Elder Glowmite', 402161, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402161, 6, 1, 'Glowmites slowly grow larger as they age. This one has lived a long, full life.', -1, 0),
(402162, 15, 5, 'Cyan Glowmite', 402162, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402162, 6, 1, 'Glowmites are well-known in the Ringing Deeps for making surprisingly sturdy mounts. This specimen produces a soft cyan glow that kobolds find especially relaxing.', -1, 0),
(402165, 15, 5, 'Soaring Meaderbee', 402165, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402165, 6, 1, 'This humble bee dreams of open skies. Whether or not an adventurer is along for the ride is of no consequence to it.', -1, 0),
(402167, 15, 5, 'Raging Cinderbee', 402167, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402167, 6, 1, 'Temper as hot as its flames, this breed of cinderbee can only be tamed by those who share its insatiable penchant for violence.', -1, 0),
(402171, 15, 5, 'Widow\'s Undercrawler', 402171, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402171, 6, 1, 'Surface-dwelling children often profess desires for a pony or wolf of their own upon reaching certain milestones of age. A young Widow Arak\'nai had similar ambitions, though her tastes would likely be considered eclectic by some standards.', -1, 0),
(402172, 15, 5, 'Heritage Undercrawler', 402172, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402172, 6, 1, 'Arachnid husbandry is a time-honored tradition amongst the Heritage Forces. Though most specimens are used for transport labor or raised to serve as shock troops, the finest examples of their brood are occasionally trained as parade mounts.', -1, 0),
(402174, 15, 5, 'Royal Court Undercrawler', 402174, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402174, 6, 1, 'Patents of lineage are used to demarcate the history and value of thoroughbred undercrawlers in Kaheti high society. This practice can prove somewhat difficult when said undercrawlers are prone to the sudden consumption of their record-keepers.', -1, 0),
(402176, 15, 5, 'Alunira', 402176, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402176, 6, 1, 'For so long, the very embodiment of the clouds laid trapped atop a mountain of lightning. And at last, I can feel the wind at my back once again.', -1, 0),
(402177, 15, 5, 'Aquamarine Swarmite', 402177, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402177, 6, 1, 'While it\'s not exactly common, the representatives of the Severed Threads assure you that swarmites are more than capable of carrying your weight if you choose to ride it.', -1, 0),
(402178, 15, 5, 'Nesting Swarmite', 402178, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402178, 6, 1, 'Burrowers by nature they often lurk in small animal warrens when laying eggs or lying in wait to surprise larger prey.', -1, 0),
(402180, 15, 5, 'Shadowed Swarmite', 402180, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402180, 6, 1, 'Swarmites are a common sight both in the wilds of Azj-Kahet and among the nerubians who have long domesticated them, but that doesn\'t make them any less dangerous to incautious adventurers.', -1, 0),
(402181, 15, 5, 'Swarmite Skyhunter', 402181, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402181, 6, 1, 'Typically found in the smallest nooks and crannies of rock ceilings, the swarmite skyhunter is more at home in the air than at rest.', -1, 0),
(402184, 15, 5, 'Ferocious Jawcrawler', 402184, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402184, 6, 1, 'This particularly large jawcrawler is the perfect size to make a mount... just keep your hands and feet clear of its mouth.', -1, 0),
(402187, 15, 5, 'Underlight Shorestalker', 402187, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402187, 6, 1, 'Aid your deep sea charger in its hunt for prey along the ocean floors.', -1, 0),
(402188, 15, 5, 'Kah, Legend of the Deep', 402188, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402188, 6, 1, '', -1, 0),
(402189, 15, 5, 'Underlight Corrupted Behemoth', 402189, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402189, 6, 1, 'The light from the saddle helps attract prey to this corrupted behemoth.', -1, 0),
(402190, 15, 5, 'Shadow of Doubt', 402190, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402190, 6, 1, 'Manifesting after Xal\'atath\'s disappearance, this shadow\'s very existence begs the question: Were her schemes truly thwarted? Or have we just played deeper into her hands?', -1, 0),
(402191, 15, 5, 'Shackled Shadow', 402191, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402191, 6, 1, 'Who would have guessed that a shadow elemental would make for such a comfortable ride?', -1, 0),
(402192, 15, 5, 'Beledar\'s Spawn', 402192, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402192, 6, 1, 'Through the Sacred Flame, whispers of dark carry you to battle.', -1, 0),
(402193, 15, 5, 'Vermillion Imperial Lynx', 402193, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402193, 6, 1, 'Imperial lynxes are considered to be an Arathi\'s greatest companion, both on and off the battlefield. Sadly, this lynx\'s previous owner died in battle.', -1, 0),
(402194, 15, 5, 'Dauntless Imperial Lynx', 402194, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402194, 6, 1, 'This lynx\'s barding has had most of its insignia ripped off. The one remaining tag reads, "Dauntless".', -1, 0),
(402198, 15, 5, 'Kor\'kron Warsaber', 402198, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402198, 6, 1, 'Finding a litter of nightsaber kittens, a squad of Kor\'kron Outriders trained them into a formidable pack of deadly mounts.', -1, 0),
(402199, 15, 5, 'Blackrock Warsaber', 402199, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402199, 6, 1, 'Finding a litter of nightsaber kittens, a squad of Blackrock Outriders trained them into a formidable pack of deadly mounts.', -1, 0),
(402201, 15, 5, 'Sentinel War Wolf', 402201, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402201, 6, 1, 'Captured in a Sentinel raid, the loyalty of the wolf favors the strongest.', -1, 0),
(402203, 15, 5, 'Kaldorei War Wolf', 402203, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402203, 6, 1, 'Captured in a Kaldorei raid, the loyalty of the wolf favors the strongest.', -1, 0),
(402204, 15, 5, 'Wick', 402204, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402204, 6, 1, 'Rescued from the ruthless charge of Ol\' Waxbeard and the looming threat of The Darkness, now able to nibble on loose wax in peace.', -1, 0),
(402205, 15, 5, 'Ol\' Mole Rufus', 402205, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402205, 6, 1, 'Wiser than words can say and still quick on his feet. He just gets a lil\' tired sometimes.', -1, 0),
(402209, 15, 5, 'Crimson Mudnose', 402209, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402209, 6, 1, 'Frequently used by kobolds as mounts, the Assembly of the Deeps has decided to allow you access to one of their most loyal mudnoses.', -1, 0),
(402211, 15, 5, 'Vicious Skyflayer', 402211, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402211, 6, 1, 'This creature hungers for battle with the contemptible Horde.', -1, 0),
(402213, 15, 5, 'Shale Ramolith', 402213, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402213, 6, 1, 'Earthen have long used ramoliths as beasts of burden due to their hardy nature. Shale ramoliths are considered to be friendlier than most others, though that isn\'t saying much.', -1, 0),
(402214, 15, 5, 'Slatestone Ramolith', 402214, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402214, 6, 1, 'Earthen ranchers talk often of this creature\'s resilience and how the rain ricochets off of its lustrous coat.', -1, 0),
(402218, 15, 5, 'Forged Gladiator\'s Fel Bat', 402218, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402218, 6, 1, 'Awakened from caves in the battlefield, and armored to the fray.', -1, 0),
(402219, 15, 5, 'Sureki Skyrazor', 402219, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402219, 6, 1, 'The skyrazor was one of the most vicious abominations to emerge from Queen Ansurek\'s experiments with the Black Blood of the Old Gods.', -1, 0),
(402220, 15, 5, 'Retrained Skyrazor', 402220, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402220, 6, 1, 'One of a handful of skyrazors captured by Arathi forces during the Sureki offensive after Queen Ansurek\'s downfall, this beast has found great use in sniffing out void corruption at home and abroad.', -1, 0),
(402222, 15, 5, 'Siesbarg', 402222, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402222, 6, 1, 'Poor guy.', -1, 0),
(402223, 15, 5, 'Ascendant Skyrazor', 402223, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402223, 6, 1, 'Intended for the most devoted of the Sureki elite, these skyrazors were favored by Queen Ansurek for both their cunning and brutality.', -1, 0),
(402224, 15, 5, 'Frayfeather Hippogryph', 402224, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402224, 6, 1, 'This majestic hippogryph hails from the Frayfeather Highlands of Feralas. Though it previously protected its hatchlings, now it chooses to serve a greater cause.', -1, 0),
(402225, 15, 5, 'Amani Hunting Bear', 402225, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402225, 6, 1, 'The Amani trolls ride this fierce creature on ceremonial hunts in honor of the bear god Nalorakk.', -1, 0),
(402230, 15, 5, 'Ivory Goliathus', 402230, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402230, 6, 1, 'These giant beetles spend their lives in the darkest tunnels of Khaz Algar. Though they are deprived even of the faintest glimmer of artificial sunlight, they still thrive.', -1, 0),
(402232, 15, 5, 'Savage Ebony Battle Turtle', 402232, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402232, 6, 1, 'The cannons are powered by an unquenchable rage to seek out enemies and bring them to justice. Nothing can outrun a cannon.', -1, 0),
(402233, 15, 5, 'Earthen Ordinant\'s Ramolith', 402233, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402233, 6, 1, 'Beneath the stone surface beats a heart emboldened by order to set this world free from darkness.', -1, 0),
(402235, 15, 5, 'Startouched Furline', 402235, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402235, 6, 1, 'An early eternal traveler encountered the furline and befriended a pair. Accompanying the traveler back to their domain, these furline kittens were forever changed by living there and accompanying the travelers.', -1, 0),
(402237, 15, 5, 'Grizzly Hills Packmaster', 402237, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402237, 6, 1, 'Traders quickly found them a very capable ally when facing the dangers of Northrend and beyond. They also learned that the bears of the Grizzly Hills were fiercely loyal. Especially to those who keep Emperor salmon at hand.', -1, 0),
(402238, 15, 5, 'Plunderlord\'s Golden Crocolisk', 402238, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402238, 6, 1, 'What is a Plunderlord without a proper display of plunder?', -1, 0),
(402239, 15, 5, 'Keg Leg\'s Radiant Crocolisk', 402239, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402239, 6, 1, 'The pirate captain later known as Keg Leg knew the risks when he rode a hungry crocolisk into battle.', -1, 0),
(402240, 15, 5, 'Plunderlord\'s Midnight Crocolisk', 402240, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402240, 6, 1, 'Any captain worth their salt knows to have a trustworthy navi-gator.', -1, 0),
(402241, 15, 5, 'Plunderlord\'s Weathered Crocolisk', 402241, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402241, 6, 1, '', -1, 0),
(402244, 15, 5, 'Diamond Mechsuit', 402244, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402244, 6, 1, 'These crystal-powered mechsuits are the epitome of Earthen technology.', -1, 0),
(402249, 15, 5, 'Hand of Reshkigaal', 402249, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402249, 6, 1, 'Reshkigaal bided her time as her kin each tried their hand at usurping the Banished One. She sought to attack when he was distracted, but the Jailer\'s spies had been tracking her. With their warning and aid, the Jailer prevailed.', -1, 0),
(402255, 15, 5, 'Golden Ashes of Al\'ar', 402255, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402255, 6, 1, 'The golden Al\'ar, beloved pet of Kael\'thas Sunstrider, proves that death is merely a setback.', -1, 0),
(402259, 15, 5, 'Gigantic Grrloc', 402259, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402259, 6, 1, 'It\'s the third biggest murloc you\'ve ever seen!', -1, 0),
(402261, 15, 5, 'Coldflame Tempest', 402261, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402261, 6, 1, 'Emerging from the chaos of the early elemental wars on Azeroth, the Coldflame Tempest is a reminder that the chill of a blizzard is eternal.', -1, 0),
(402262, 15, 5, 'Harmonious Salutations Bear', 402262, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402262, 6, 1, 'Riding this mount fills you with a stillness and peace that is not frequently known to accompany murlocs or bears.', -1, 0),
(402265, 15, 5, 'Trader\'s Gilded Brutosaur', 402265, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402265, 6, 1, 'Morten and Killia never realized how much their new trading partnership across faction lines would pay off. That is until the day they were able to purchase this fine creature to aid them in their travels. And of course do it in gilded style.', -1, 0),
(402272, 15, 5, 'Crimson Armored Growler', 402272, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402272, 6, 1, 'Some Goblins affectionately refer to trained hyenas as \'Growlers.\' This one is fond of digging.', -1, 0),
(402274, 15, 5, 'Blackwater Bonecrusher', 402274, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402274, 6, 1, 'Best keep those bones to yourself if you don\'t want them crushed.', -1, 0),
(402276, 15, 5, 'Darkfuse Chompactor', 402276, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402276, 6, 1, 'Considered the Top Dog among Stix\'s Junkyard Hyenas, it boasts a bite force strong enough to crush whatever - or whoever - Gallywix wants disposed of.', -1, 0),
(402277, 15, 5, 'Violet Armored Growler', 402277, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402277, 6, 1, 'Smaks knows a thing or two about caring for hyenas. Rule number one: keep your hands away from those teeth!', -1, 0),
(402278, 15, 5, 'Flarendo the Furious', 402278, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402278, 6, 1, 'Being the VIP of VIPs at the Gallagio has its perks, including the keys to this former King of Carnage. Cutting-edge goblin technology allows him to achieve over 100 yards per gallon!', -1, 0),
(402279, 15, 5, 'Thunderdrum Misfire', 402279, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402279, 6, 1, 'Recovered from the Cauldron\'s bleachers during a particularly gruesome clash. When asked if it was a dud, Torq\'s operator simply replied: \'Probably?\'', -1, 0),
(402280, 15, 5, 'The Topskimmer Special', 402280, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402280, 6, 1, 'Smaks is sure this rocket won\'t explode mid-flight. Absolutely. Positively. 100%. Sure.', -1, 0),
(402281, 15, 5, 'Steamwheedle Supplier', 402281, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402281, 6, 1, 'Supplies you with a quick trip, or your enemies with a large explosion!', -1, 0),
(402283, 15, 5, 'Innovation Investigator', 402283, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402283, 6, 1, 'When the best path to a good idea is going really fast.', -1, 0),
(402284, 15, 5, 'Ochre Delivery Rocket', 402284, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402284, 6, 1, 'Get packages and passengers from point A to B in style!', -1, 0),
(402286, 15, 5, 'Blackwater Shredder Deluxe Mk 2', 402286, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402286, 6, 1, 'Best not to ask what happened to Mk 1.', -1, 0),
(402287, 15, 5, 'Darkfuse Demolisher', 402287, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402287, 6, 1, 'Excellent at making a mess of things. Not so great at cleaning them up.', -1, 0),
(402288, 15, 5, 'Personalized Goblin S.C.R.A.P.per', 402288, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402288, 6, 1, 'Goblin Shredders have proven time and again to be useful in many applications, such as in logging and transportation. This model has been repurposed for use by S.C.R.A.P..', -1, 0),
(402289, 15, 5, 'Venture Co-ordinator', 402289, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402289, 6, 1, 'Built to manage any Venture-related operation from the front lines.', -1, 0),
(402290, 15, 5, 'Asset Advocator', 402290, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402290, 6, 1, 'Assuring others that your assets are exactly where they should be.', -1, 0),
(402291, 15, 5, 'Salvaged Goblin Gazillionaire\'s Flying Machine', 402291, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402291, 6, 1, 'Once the prized possession of elite goblin society, this flying machine was sadly relegated to the scrap heap after something bigger, brighter, and more explosive arrived on the market.', -1, 0),
(402292, 15, 5, 'Margin Manipulator', 402292, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402292, 6, 1, 'Ensuring there is always some marginal distance between you and rock bottom.', -1, 0),
(402293, 15, 5, 'Darkfuse Spy-Eye', 402293, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402293, 6, 1, 'Perfect for the up-and-comer who wants to climb the ladder by making everyone else\'s business THEIR business.', -1, 0),
(402294, 15, 5, 'Mean Green Flying Machine', 402294, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402294, 6, 1, 'Steamwheedle\'s top engineers claim they invented this work of mechanical genius, while the other cartels copied their plans.', -1, 0),
(402295, 15, 5, 'Bilgewater Bombardier', 402295, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402295, 6, 1, 'For rapid transport of Cartel trade goods and other highly volatile substances.', -1, 0),
(402296, 15, 5, 'Delver\'s Gob-Trotter', 402296, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402296, 6, 1, 'This aircraft will help you delve straight into adventure, if it doesn\'t explode!', -1, 0),
(402298, 15, 5, 'Prized Gladiator\'s Fel Bat', 402298, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402298, 6, 1, 'Awakened from caves in the battlefield, and armored to the fray.', -1, 0),
(402299, 15, 5, 'Vicious Electro Eel', 402299, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402299, 6, 1, 'These aquatic beasts enjoy torturing the Alliance with their electric shocks.', -1, 0),
(402300, 15, 5, 'Vicious Electro Eel', 402300, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402300, 6, 1, 'These aquatic beasts enjoy torturing the Horde with their electric shocks.', -1, 0),
(402301, 15, 5, 'Unstable Rocket', 402301, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402301, 6, 1, 'What it lacks in safety features it more than makes up for in speed and style. Not for the faint of heart.', -1, 0),
(402303, 15, 5, 'Violet Goblin Shredder', 402303, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402303, 6, 1, 'This shredder has been lovingly painted with a non-corrosive paint to ensure a lasting sheen.', -1, 0),
(402304, 15, 5, 'Chaos-Forged Gryphon', 402304, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402304, 6, 1, 'Born and raised during a time of great chaos, this mount has survived hardships known by few.', -1, 0);
INSERT INTO `item_template` (`entry`, `class`, `subclass`, `name`, `displayid`, `Quality`, `Flags`, `BuyPrice`, `SellPrice`, `ItemLevel`, `RequiredSkill`, `RequiredSkillRank`, `delay`, `spellid_1`, `spellcharges_1`, `spellid_2`, `spelltrigger_2`, `bonding`, `description`, `Material`, `BagFamily`) VALUES
(402305, 15, 5, 'Chaos-Forged Hippogryph', 402305, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402305, 6, 1, 'Born and raised during a time of great chaos, this mount has survived hardships known by few.', -1, 0),
(402307, 15, 5, 'Chaos-Forged Dreadwing', 402307, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402307, 6, 1, 'Born and raised during a time of great chaos, this mount has survived hardships known by few.', -1, 0),
(402308, 15, 5, 'Chaos-Forged Wind Rider', 402308, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402308, 6, 1, 'Born and raised during a time of great chaos, this mount has survived hardships known by few.', -1, 0),
(402313, 15, 5, 'Junkmaestro\'s Magnetomech', 402313, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402313, 6, 1, 'Well-suited for compacting trash into rollable balls. Junkmaestro apocrypha claims these might become worlds of their own if only they could get big enough.', -1, 0),
(402315, 15, 5, 'Timbered Sky Snake', 402315, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402315, 6, 1, 'A living, breathing, flying work of art.', -1, 0),
(402317, 15, 5, 'Enchanted Spellweave Carpet', 402317, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402317, 6, 1, 'Dalaran mages have created an elegant spellweave and self-stitch aura to accompany this flying carpet. Allowing anyone to handle any loose threads and fly in style.', -1, 0),
(402321, 15, 5, 'Timely Buzzbee', 402321, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402321, 6, 1, 'Buzzing through the time punctual as ever, these Buzzbees harvest the errant sands of time and return them safely to the Timeways.', -1, 0),
(402322, 15, 5, 'Thrayir, Eyes of the Siren', 402322, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402322, 6, 1, 'In a fit of rage and despair, Thrayir conjured a storm that would ravage the land and annihilate Cyrce\'s enemies. After nearly ten thousand years, the seafury tempest continues to roil as an echo of his power.', -1, 0),
(402324, 15, 5, 'Hooktalon', 402324, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402324, 6, 1, 'Hooktalon once sailed with the Bloodsail Buccaneers, and later with the Blackwater Raiders, but he left to see what plunder he could find beyond the high seas.', -1, 0),
(402326, 15, 5, 'Astral Gladiator\'s Fel Bat', 402326, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402326, 6, 1, 'Awakened from caves in the battlefield, and armored to the fray.', -1, 0),
(402327, 15, 5, 'Lunar Launcher', 402327, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402327, 6, 1, 'It\'s always a festival when you are on the Lunar Launcher.', -1, 0),
(402328, 15, 5, 'Love Witch\'s Sweeper', 402328, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402328, 6, 1, 'The original design of the feeling-fueled magic broom series "Motion By Emotion", this ride is sure to get you there in a swiffy!', -1, 0),
(402329, 15, 5, 'Silvermoon Sweeper', 402329, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402329, 6, 1, 'The Silvermoon color scheme for the "Motion By Emotion" has been a success all across Azeroth.', -1, 0),
(402330, 15, 5, 'Twilight Witch\'s Sweeper', 402330, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402330, 6, 1, 'A darker look for the "Motion By Emotion" magic broom series of mounts. Fans of this color know that it looks good regardless of the time of day.', -1, 0),
(402331, 15, 5, 'Sky Witch\'s Sweeper', 402331, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402331, 6, 1, 'The sky\'s the limit when you mount up on this "Motion By Emotion" magic broom model.', -1, 0),
(402332, 15, 5, 'The Breaker\'s Song', 402332, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402332, 6, 1, '\'Tis a rare moment in history when a sailor carves the very monster that left \'em stranded to die upon the bow of their ship. Our lot is a blasphemous and piddly bunch. To think one of us might have the humility to honor such a creature is damn near mad.', -1, 0),
(402333, 15, 5, 'Soweezi\'s Vintage Waveshredder', 402333, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402333, 6, 1, 'This pretty lil\' thing has a beautiful platinum sheen. It\'ll take ya sky-high in seconds! You\'ll be dancing around the sun to your heart\'s content for the low, low price of ten thousand smackeroonies.', -1, 0),
(402334, 15, 5, 'Bronze Goblin Waveshredder', 402334, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402334, 6, 1, 'Even cartel employees deserve to have some R&R on occassion.', -1, 0),
(402347, 15, 5, 'Savage Alabaster Battle Turtle', 402347, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402347, 6, 1, 'Wisdom throughout the ages has led to a well-known saying, "Nothing can outrun a cannon."', -1, 0),
(402469, 15, 5, 'Prismatic Snapdragon', 402469, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402469, 6, 1, 'Chameleonic creatures can oftentimes adapt their cells to match the color of the outside world. This snapdragon adopted this ability, but only to match the contents of their stomach; taking the phrase \'you are what you eat\' to a whole new level.', -1, 0),
(402470, 15, 5, 'Nightfall Skyreaver', 402470, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402470, 6, 1, 'Descending on their prey in the dead of night, the cries of these skyreavers once instilled terror in all the children of Draenor.', -1, 0),
(402471, 15, 5, 'Ur\'zul Fleshripper', 402471, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402471, 6, 1, 'This terrifying ur\'zul incorporates its latest victims into itself, creating a nearly unstoppable monster. Good thing you are treating it well, or you might be its next treat.', -1, 0),
(402473, 15, 5, 'Broodling of Sinestra', 402473, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402473, 6, 1, 'After the fall of the Bastion of Twilight, a few scattered twilight whelps escaped Vexiona\'s sway. Some of these whelps have allied with mortals and are willing to bear them as riders.', -1, 0),
(402474, 15, 5, 'Copper-Maned Quilen', 402474, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402474, 6, 1, 'Raised in the stables of the Iron Qon, these mounts are ardently steadfast, never leaving their posts even when they sensed the demise of their masters.', -1, 0),
(402476, 15, 5, 'Sha-Warped Cloud Serpent', 402476, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402476, 6, 1, 'Sha has warped this cloud serpent into an even more fearsome creature. The emotions that flow through this creature make it an unmistakable harbinger of doom.', -1, 0),
(402477, 15, 5, 'Sha-Warped Riding Tiger', 402477, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402477, 6, 1, 'Sha has warped this tiger into an even more fearsome creature. The emotions that flow through this creature make it an unmistakable harbinger of doom.', -1, 0),
(402478, 15, 5, 'Blazing Royal Fire Hawk', 402478, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402478, 6, 1, 'Only the most passionate of souls and fiercest of hearts can claim the Blazing Royal Fire Hawk as a mount.', -1, 0),
(402480, 15, 5, 'Crimson Shreddertank', 402480, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402480, 6, 1, 'Experimental shredder designed for killing rather than harvesting.', -1, 0),
(402481, 15, 5, 'Midnight Darkmoon Charger', 402481, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402481, 6, 1, '', -1, 0),
(402482, 15, 5, 'Lively Darkmoon Charger', 402482, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402482, 6, 1, 'Draped in tattered circus banners, this eerie mount is a perfect blend of shadow and spectacle.', -1, 0),
(402483, 15, 5, 'Violet Darkmoon Charger', 402483, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402483, 6, 1, 'This steed carries the mystery and magic of the Darkmoon Faire on its back.', -1, 0),
(402484, 15, 5, 'Snowy Darkmoon Charger', 402484, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402484, 6, 1, '', -1, 0),
(402487, 15, 5, 'The Big G', 402487, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402487, 6, 1, 'Doesn\'t actually seem like anything too special under the hood, but just wait until those goblins next door see you pull up for the next pool party.', -1, 0),
(402488, 15, 5, 'Shimmermist Free Runner', 402488, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402488, 6, 1, 'Unburdened from the saddle and bit, these valerunners are truly free.', -1, 0),
(402489, 15, 5, 'Pearlescent Butterfly', 402489, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402489, 6, 1, 'Take to the skies on a glittering, shimmering, pearlescent butterfly.', -1, 0),
(402491, 15, 5, 'Ruby Butterfly', 402491, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402491, 6, 1, 'The elusive Ruby Butterfly is highly sought after by Twilight Witches.', -1, 0),
(402492, 15, 5, 'Spring Butterfly', 402492, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402492, 6, 1, 'Take to the skies on a glittering, shimmering, spring butterfly.', -1, 0),
(402494, 15, 5, 'Midnight Butterfly', 402494, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402494, 6, 1, 'PH', -1, 0),
(402495, 15, 5, 'Emerald Snail', 402495, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402495, 6, 1, 'This snail protects its treasures with the ferocity of a dragon, but perhaps not the speed.', -1, 0),
(402496, 15, 5, 'Void-Scarred Gryphon', 402496, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402496, 6, 1, 'Abandoned by its trainers the Void-Scarred Gryphon scrounged on any scrap of food that remained, most corrupted by the void.', -1, 0),
(402497, 15, 5, 'Void-Forged Stallion', 402497, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402497, 6, 1, 'Forged just as their shoes once were, these beasts are less horses now and void energy in their likeness.', -1, 0),
(402498, 15, 5, 'Void-Scarred Pack Mother', 402498, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402498, 6, 1, 'Fighting her corrupted handlers this pack mother freed herself and her pups. However, freedom from their handlers did not free them from the void in this lost place.', -1, 0),
(402499, 15, 5, 'Void-Scarred Windrider', 402499, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402499, 6, 1, 'When the void energies were released, it drove most windriders feral. They killed each other and their trainers. The gates to their roost were locked by the survivors.', -1, 0),
(402500, 15, 5, 'Ny\'alothan Shadow Worm', 402500, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402500, 6, 1, 'A remnant of the Black Empire\'s past, these precursors of the abyss worms are once again resurging with the rise of Ny\'alotha.', -1, 0),
(402501, 15, 5, 'Corruption of the Aspects', 402501, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402501, 6, 1, 'With N\'Zoth\'s triumph, what started with Galakrond comes to fruition. With the Aspects gone, the corruption of their species is complete.', -1, 0),
(402502, 15, 5, 'Void-Crystal Panther', 402502, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402502, 6, 1, 'Although many precious gems have been corrupted by void energies in horrific visions, Master Jewelcrafters can still utilize them to craft mighty panther steeds.', -1, 0),
(402504, 15, 5, 'Spotted Black Riding Goat', 402504, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402504, 6, 1, 'One time a farmhand walked by without petting this goat. That\'s all it took for the goat to make it personal.', -1, 0),
(402505, 15, 5, 'Resplendent K\'arroc', 402505, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402505, 6, 1, 'A technological marvel in the flesh, this K\'arroc represents hope for a brighter K\'aresh.', -1, 0),
(402507, 15, 5, 'Prototype A.S.M.R.', 402507, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402507, 6, 1, 'Representing the pinnacle of goblin propaganda technology, Gallywix commissioned the Automatic Sonic Machine Resonator to sway his most stubborn critics.', -1, 0),
(402508, 15, 5, 'Enterprising Shreddertank', 402508, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402508, 6, 1, 'Optimized shredder designed for maximum shredding efficiency.', -1, 0),
(402510, 15, 5, 'Terror of the Wastes', 402510, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402510, 6, 1, 'It\'s not world-devouringly bad, just misunderstood.', -1, 0),
(402511, 15, 5, 'Terror of the Night', 402511, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402511, 6, 1, 'Don\'t be deceived by its bright colors, it is capable of sneaking up on anyone (or anything).', -1, 0),
(402512, 15, 5, 'Delver\'s Mana-Skimmer', 402512, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402512, 6, 1, 'This aircraft will help you delve straight into adventure, or maybe other dimensions!', -1, 0),
(402518, 15, 5, 'Chrono Corsair', 402518, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402518, 6, 1, 'Always on the lookout for the next golden opportunity, this Infinite Dragonflight pirate has soared through the timeways to find a crew for the perfect heist.', -1, 0),
(402519, 15, 5, 'Radiant Imperial Lynx', 402519, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402519, 6, 1, 'The Radiant Imperial Lynx embodies the ongoing strength and courage it takes to chase back the darkness. They hoist us up so that we may hold our torches high for all who seek refuge from the encroaching darkness.', -1, 0),
(402520, 15, 5, 'Spring Harvesthog', 402520, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402520, 6, 1, 'The Spring Harvesthog is at its most energetic in the early morning. It will spend most of its day snuffling for food or bellowing out calls for other harvesthogs.', -1, 0),
(402521, 15, 5, 'Summer Harvesthog', 402521, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402521, 6, 1, 'The Summer Harvesthog enjoys laying out in the sun or going for a swim in a clear lake. They are excellent at foraging for food, but need to be coaxed into it.', -1, 0),
(402522, 15, 5, 'Winter Harvesthog', 402522, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402522, 6, 1, 'Winter Harvesthogs are primarily nocturnal creatures. They are slightly slower than other harvesthogs, but their endurance is unmatched.', -1, 0),
(402523, 15, 5, 'Autumn Harvesthog', 402523, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402523, 6, 1, 'Autumn Harvesthogs excel in snuffling for food in the cooler months. Their keen sense of smell makes them excellent companions for a forrest forage, but difficult to control in aromatic settings.', -1, 0),
(402524, 15, 5, 'Coldflame Cormaera', 402524, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402524, 6, 1, 'During the war of the elemental lords, Cormaera were often used as beasts of burden for the Firelord\'s most loyal lieutenants.', -1, 0),
(402525, 15, 5, 'Prophet\'s Great Raven', 402525, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402525, 6, 1, 'As the Prophet, Medivh delivered his missives in the form of a black raven. Although not as impressive as shapeshifting, this bird still carries all the prestige of its namesake.', -1, 0),
(402526, 15, 5, 'Felborn Cormaera', 402526, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402526, 6, 1, 'Cormaera were an early species on Azeroth that were claimed by elemental lords.', -1, 0),
(402527, 15, 5, 'Molten Cormaera', 402527, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402527, 6, 1, 'In the earliest days of Azeroth, these elemental predators dominated the inferno-choked skies of Ragnaros\'s domain.', -1, 0),
(402528, 15, 5, 'Lavaborn Cormaera', 402528, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402528, 6, 1, 'Under the eye of the elemental lords, many cormaera were twisted by their forces and became loyal mounts and partners.', -1, 0),
(402529, 15, 5, 'Archmage\'s Great Raven', 402529, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402529, 6, 1, 'Perhaps a little older and a bit more gray instead of customary darkened midnight, this raven still represents one of the most powerful arcane masters of Azeroth, the Guardian Khadgar.', -1, 0),
(402531, 15, 5, 'Tyrannotort', 402531, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402531, 6, 1, 'Vinnie Sweets kept this rare, albino turtle a secret, saving until it was time to help promote Dastardly Duos.', -1, 0),
(402532, 15, 5, 'Herald of Sa\'bak', 402532, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402532, 6, 1, 'The Tol\'vir tell of the legendary Sa\'bak, a great crocolisk believed to have emerged from the sacred valley of Un\'Goro crater.', -1, 0),
(402535, 15, 5, 'Void-Scarred Lynx', 402535, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402535, 6, 1, 'Taming lynxes is a practice that the Arathi have honed for years. While the Nightfall cultists remain devoted to their cause, they are still ones for passing that tradition along.', -1, 0),
(402542, 15, 5, 'Bloodhunter Fel Bat', 402542, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402542, 6, 1, 'A beast from an unknown world within the Twisting Nether, tamed through brutal and relentless will.', -1, 0),
(402544, 15, 5, 'Ashplague Fel Bat', 402544, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402544, 6, 1, 'Only the mightiest of heroes ride into battle atop this monstrosity borne of fel and undeath.', -1, 0),
(402546, 15, 5, 'Wretched Fel Bat', 402546, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402546, 6, 1, 'Its bracers seem to be a bit snug.', -1, 0),
(402549, 15, 5, 'Umbral K\'arroc', 402549, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402549, 6, 1, 'A savage K\'arroc particularly well-suited to prowling the perpetual twilight of K\'aresh.', -1, 0),
(402550, 15, 5, 'K\'arroc Swiftwing', 402550, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402550, 6, 1, 'A gift for services rendered, this K\'arroc has seen its share of hazardous flights.', -1, 0),
(402552, 15, 5, 'Lavender K\'arroc', 402552, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402552, 6, 1, 'This particularly belligerent K\'arroc\'s previous master died while investigating Untethered Space. Perhaps it will accept you instead... or maybe not.', -1, 0),
(402555, 15, 5, 'The Bone Freezer', 402555, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402555, 6, 1, 'Bitter rival to The Bone Melter, this creeper was ousted from their lair near Manaforge Omega after a crushing defeat. It now seeks to learn from the one that dethroned its greatest foe.', -1, 0),
(402556, 15, 5, 'Ruby Void Creeper', 402556, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402556, 6, 1, 'Rescued by the K\'aresh Trust for study, this void creeper has turned out to be an incredibly sturdy mount.', -1, 0),
(402557, 15, 5, 'Acidic Void Creeper', 402557, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402557, 6, 1, 'This creeper has feasted on noxious fumes resulting in its body being infused with powerful acids.', -1, 0),
(402560, 15, 5, 'Blue Barry', 402560, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402560, 6, 1, 'A particularly rare variant of slateback, "Blue Barry" was previously used as a beast of burden.', -1, 0),
(402561, 15, 5, 'Curious Slateback', 402561, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402561, 6, 1, 'This curious slateback somehow managed to get itself stuck in a box. How it fit inside is still up in the air.', -1, 0),
(402566, 15, 5, 'Lana\'thel\'s Crimson Cascade', 402566, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402566, 6, 1, 'The Blood Queen\'s mastery of the sanguine arts allowed her to conjure a fearsome servant to bear her into battle.', -1, 0),
(402567, 15, 5, 'Voidwing Dragonhawk', 402567, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402567, 6, 1, 'Cutting through the skies, it flies with silent wings and eyes that glow with the echo of forgotten stars.', -1, 0),
(402568, 15, 5, 'Lightwing Dragonhawk', 402568, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402568, 6, 1, 'Radiating warmth and grace, it soars on wings of light.', -1, 0),
(402569, 15, 5, 'Unbound Star-Eater', 402569, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402569, 6, 1, 'In the void-scarred wake of the All-Devouring and his kith, twisted remnants of distant worlds and forgotten aeons find their way across the Great Dark.', -1, 0),
(402570, 15, 5, 'Vicious Void Creeper', 402570, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402570, 6, 1, 'Originating from K\'aresh, these creatures like to burrow and ambush unsuspecting Horde.', -1, 0),
(402571, 15, 5, 'Vicious Void Creeper', 402571, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402571, 6, 1, 'Originating from K\'aresh, these creatures like to burrow and ambush unsuspecting Alliance.', -1, 0),
(402572, 15, 5, 'Banshee\'s Chilling Charger', 402572, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402572, 6, 1, '', -1, 0),
(402573, 15, 5, 'Grandiose Grrloc', 402573, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402573, 6, 1, 'It\'s the fourth biggest murloc you\'ve ever seen!', -1, 0),
(402574, 15, 5, 'Snowy Highmountain Eagle', 402574, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402574, 6, 1, 'To find the feather of a snowy eagle in Highmountain is an omen of shifting winds and temperature drops.', -1, 0),
(402575, 15, 5, 'Grandmaster\'s Prophetic Board', 402575, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402575, 6, 1, 'The chess event was not to be contained. So Medivh fashioned this conveyance to take it on trips.', -1, 0),
(402576, 15, 5, 'Grandmaster\'s Deep Board', 402576, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402576, 6, 1, '', -1, 0),
(402577, 15, 5, 'Grandmaster\'s Royal Board', 402577, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402577, 6, 1, 'Always moving forward to position yourself above the pawns below.', -1, 0),
(402578, 15, 5, 'Grandmaster\'s Smokey Board', 402578, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402578, 6, 1, '', -1, 0),
(402579, 15, 5, 'Forsaken\'s Grotesque Charger', 402579, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402579, 6, 1, 'A corpse is a corpse, of course of course.', -1, 0),
(402580, 15, 5, 'Wailing Banshee\'s Charger', 402580, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402580, 6, 1, 'These shadow-graced steeds silently carry the Priests of the Forgotten Shadow through the darkened woods of Tirisfal.', -1, 0),
(402581, 15, 5, 'Banshee\'s Sickening Charger', 402581, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402581, 6, 1, '', -1, 0),
(402582, 15, 5, 'Shaohao\'s Sage Serpent', 402582, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402582, 6, 1, 'The lessons Shaohao learned in life and death and the passion he held for his home have coalesced into this ethereal serpent, a reflection of the Emperor\'s wisdom.', -1, 0),
(402586, 15, 5, 'Moonlit Nightsaber', 402586, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402586, 6, 1, 'Her white glow upon their silvered fur, her bright-blue gaze in their moonlit eyes. Oh, how the moons smile on these creatures. -Mother Kalo\'thera, High Priestess of Elune, A Blessing in Hajiri', -1, 0),
(402587, 15, 5, 'Ivory Savagemane', 402587, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402587, 6, 1, 'According to Raptari legend, during Dazar\'s first ascent up the slopes of Zandalar, the soon-to-be-King was guided through the darkness by the shimmer of ivory scales and gleaming red eyes.', -1, 0),
(402593, 15, 5, 'Slag Basilisk', 402593, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402593, 6, 1, 'Originally dwelling deep underground where their diet consisted of obsidian and basalt, the slag basilisks surfaced when their homes were disturbed by the Legion.', -1, 0),
(402598, 15, 5, 'Voidlight Surger', 402598, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402598, 6, 1, 'Shifting between radiant light and consuming void, it surges through the skies in a dance of balance.', -1, 0),
(402600, 15, 5, 'Unarmored Deathtusk Felboar', 402600, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402600, 6, 1, 'Wandering the glades of Felwood on a steady diet of cursed truffles and lost travelers. Do not pet.', -1, 0),
(402601, 15, 5, 'Pearlescent Krolusk', 402601, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402601, 6, 1, 'Introduced as an invasive species to K\'aresh, Krolusk have found some use as beasts of burden.', -1, 0),
(402602, 15, 5, 'Translocated Gorger', 402602, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402602, 6, 1, 'Accidentally transported when the Brokers moved Tazavesh, this gorger has found a new world ripe with potential sources of energy, such as anima beacons...and riders.', -1, 0),
(402603, 15, 5, 'Sthaarbs\'s Last Lunch', 402603, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402603, 6, 1, 'When one cosmically invasive threat meets another, sometimes the smaller will end up on the menu of the larger. At least cosmic observers don\'t always chew their meals.', -1, 0),
(402604, 15, 5, 'OC91 Chariot', 402604, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402604, 6, 1, 'The OC91 Chariot mechsuit is overcharged with the power of Titans. The enhanced power reportedly increases the reflexes and abilities of the pilot.', -1, 0),
(402605, 15, 5, 'Inarius\' Charger', 402605, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402605, 6, 1, 'A symbol of vengeance throughout all known realms.', -1, 0),
(402606, 15, 5, 'Royal Voidwing', 402606, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402606, 6, 1, 'A cosmic terror warped and hardened by the cruelties of the Nexus-King, now oathsworn to your service.', -1, 0),
(402607, 15, 5, 'Ashes of Belo\'ren', 402607, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402607, 6, 1, 'One of Al\'ar\'s last clutch, Belo\'ren was taken to the Isle of Quel\'Danas and raised to defend the Sunwell from any who would threaten it with his very life. It is said that death will never claim him.', -1, 0),
(402608, 15, 5, 'Light-Forged Mechsuit', 402608, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402608, 6, 1, 'Cooperation between the newly-awakened earthen Ordinants and the smiths of Hallowfall has resulted an improved, light-forged earthen mechsuit.', -1, 0),
(402611, 15, 5, 'Dusk Grimlynx', 402611, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402611, 6, 1, 'Famously adept at hunting at dusk as the light of dusk blends this grimlynx\'s foliage with its surroundings.', -1, 0),
(402612, 15, 5, 'Void-Forged Overseer', 402612, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402612, 6, 1, 'After the Sepulcher of the First Ones was opened, this construct of the First Ones was stolen by the brokers and sold to the ethereals in a transaction at the Veiled Market.', -1, 0),
(402614, 15, 5, 'Fierce Grimlynx', 402614, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402614, 6, 1, 'This grimlynx has seen many battles against the creatures in the Rift of Aln.', -1, 0),
(402615, 15, 5, 'Rootstalker Grimlynx', 402615, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402615, 6, 1, 'With fur to match the deep roots and armor to match the vast foliage, these Grimlynx are equipped to be some of the ultimate hunters of Harandar.', -1, 0),
(402616, 15, 5, 'Ivory Grimlynx', 402616, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402616, 6, 1, 'Ivory grimlynxes have a strong independent streak. It takes an especially brave Haranir to ride them.', -1, 0),
(402618, 15, 5, 'Thunder-Ridged Elekk', 402618, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402618, 6, 1, 'Even infusion with demonic magics could not break the spirits of these majestic beasts, and their twisted forms were never integrated into the Legion\'s service.', -1, 0),
(402619, 15, 5, 'Cinder-Seared Elekk', 402619, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402619, 6, 1, 'The Burning Legion sought to destroy, steal or corrupt anything that brought joy to the draenei, and the elekks of Draneor were no exception.', -1, 0),
(402620, 15, 5, 'Void-Razed Elekk', 402620, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402620, 6, 1, 'Their temperament is as wild as the twisted forces that warped their creation and they only serve who they choose.', -1, 0),
(402621, 15, 5, 'Legion-Forged Elekk', 402621, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402621, 6, 1, 'The Burning Legion envied the draenei\'s bond with the elekks of Draenor. Many demonic beast-masters warped the breed to serve their needs, but none could control them.', -1, 0),
(402622, 15, 5, 'The Headless Horseman\'s Chilling Charger', 402622, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402622, 6, 1, 'Through the air you will fly, on your foes you descend, this charger will carry you to deliver their end.', -1, 0),
(402623, 15, 5, 'The Headless Horseman\'s Ghoulish Charger', 402623, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402623, 6, 1, 'Tricks have been played, your enemies beaten, this ghoulish charger awaits a treat, friend.', -1, 0),
(402624, 15, 5, 'The Headless Horseman\'s Burning Charger', 402624, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402624, 6, 1, 'The fires blaze on, in the steed\'s heart and soul, now take to the sky as a sight to behold.', -1, 0),
(402625, 15, 5, 'The Headless Horseman\'s Hallowed Charger', 402625, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402625, 6, 1, 'Your future\'s unknown, with ghosts in your past. With your steed at your side, how long can you last?', -1, 0),
(402626, 15, 5, 'Adorned Northeron Gryphon', 402626, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402626, 6, 1, 'The elder gryphon riders and high shamans of the Northeron Wildhammer often adorned their gryphons in ornate, feather-clad pieces, indicating their rank and status.', -1, 0),
(402627, 15, 5, 'High Shaman\'s Aerie Gryphon', 402627, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402627, 6, 1, 'The ancient Wildhammer shamans who first encountered gryphons believed them to be elemental spirits in mortal form. This encounter would forever imprint on the Wildhammer clan for generations to come.', -1, 0),
(402628, 15, 5, 'Cinder-Plumed Highland Gryphon', 402628, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402628, 6, 1, 'According to Wildhammer legend, the orange plumage found on gryphons is believed to be a hereditary trait passed down from their elemental ancestry.', -1, 0),
(402629, 15, 5, 'Emberwing Sky Guide', 402629, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402629, 6, 1, 'From the foothills of Khaz Modan, we followed its ember-lit wings--a northbound torch across the dark summer sky. - The Pilgrimage of the First Wildsage', -1, 0),
(402630, 15, 5, 'Ornery Breezestrider', 402630, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402630, 6, 1, 'This talbuk is a stubborn, obstinate mount, even after getting to know its rider. Riders beware.', -1, 0),
(402631, 15, 5, 'Scarlet Void Flyer', 402631, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402631, 6, 1, 'Driven mad by the void, these winged creatures are a flurry of claws and teeth.', -1, 0),
(402632, 15, 5, 'Astral Aurochs', 402632, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402632, 6, 1, 'Victory is not a simple matter of strength, but having the wisdom and ability to deliver the strength where it is needed most.', -1, 0),
(402633, 15, 5, 'Azure Void Flyer', 402633, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402633, 6, 1, 'Twisted by the void, these winged creatures now rule the skies of K\'aresh.', -1, 0),
(402634, 15, 5, 'Scorching Valor', 402634, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402634, 6, 1, 'Some cannot be held back or restrained. Scorching Valor will seek greatness and only serve those who can serve their pursuit.', -1, 0),
(402640, 15, 5, 'Brewfest Bomber', 402640, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402640, 6, 1, 'Careful not to consume the ammunition.', -1, 0),
(402645, 15, 5, 'Kalu\'ak Crest-Horn', 402645, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402645, 6, 1, 'The tuskarr do not call these Crest-Horn "Kalu\'ak" to claim them, but as a warning they will not tolerate any more lost to poachers seeking their unique antlers.', -1, 0),
(402649, 15, 5, 'Whaletested Crest-Horn', 402649, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402649, 6, 1, 'The Crest-Horn will often be drawn to graze on the plants that grow in the sea. Some have braved the fiercest wildlife there, making them true Kalu\'ak.', -1, 0),
(402650, 15, 5, 'Floestrider Crest-Horn', 402650, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402650, 6, 1, 'The seldom seen native of the Azure Span is considered blessed by the tuskaar of the region.', -1, 0),
(402651, 15, 5, 'Cragstepper Crest-Horn', 402651, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402651, 6, 1, 'Tuskaar aren\'t often found on Highmountain, but the crest-horns often come down to the shores to seek rare delicacies in the coastal waters.', -1, 0),
(402652, 15, 5, 'Bilebound Ur\'zul', 402652, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402652, 6, 1, 'This demonic amalgamation was the result of a warlock\'s experiments in curse-infused alchemy. Whether the experiment was a success or failure depends on who you ask.', -1, 0),
(402653, 15, 5, 'Ghastly Ur\'zul', 402653, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402653, 6, 1, 'A ravenous breed of demon, the ghastly ur\'zul tears through withered flesh and bone the way one would graze a salad.', -1, 0),
(402655, 15, 5, 'Phase-Lost Slateback', 402655, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402655, 6, 1, 'This Slateback got lost wandering into various phases as it followed some ethereals around.', -1, 0),
(402660, 15, 5, 'Leystone Basilisk', 402660, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402660, 6, 1, 'This beautiful basilisk is often hunted for the magical properties of its organs. Fortunately for the basilisk, its connection to ley lines gives it a prescient sense of approaching predators.', -1, 0),
(402661, 15, 5, 'Felslate Basilisk', 402661, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402661, 6, 1, 'Once common on the Broken Isles, felslate basilisks have been hunted heavily by miners seeking their precious skins.', -1, 0),
(402662, 15, 5, 'Aquamarine Basilisk', 402662, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402662, 6, 1, 'Despite their name, aquamarine basilisks feast on a variety of coastal crystals and oceanic rocks.', -1, 0),
(402663, 15, 5, 'Illidari Dreadstalker', 402663, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402663, 6, 1, 'Despite their taste for flesh and unnatural ability to smell fear, these lesser demons have been dominated by the Illidari as one would tame a hunting companion.', -1, 0),
(402664, 15, 5, 'Illidari Blightstalker', 402664, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402664, 6, 1, 'These demons devour plague and relish in decay. Who thought it would be a good idea to ride them?', -1, 0),
(402665, 15, 5, 'Highland Elderhorn', 402665, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402665, 6, 1, 'The hide of a highland elderhorn is incredibly thick. Never in recorded history has a highland elderhorn even blinked in response to insults thrown at them.', -1, 0),
(402666, 15, 5, 'Treetop Highmountain Eagle', 402666, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402666, 6, 1, 'The majestic eagle is a symbol of pride for the Highmountain tribes. This great beast\'s ability to carry tauren on their backs speaks to the sheer strength and size of the creatures of Highmountain.', -1, 0),
(402670, 15, 5, 'Arcberry Manasaber', 402670, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402670, 6, 1, 'Named for their resemblance to the bright berries made into arcwine, these proud cats have a keen awareness of the ley lines that travel beneath them.', -1, 0),
(402671, 15, 5, 'Fel-Scarred Mana Ray', 402671, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402671, 6, 1, 'Surviving on Argus is not an easy task. Its leathery hide scarred by fel corruption, this mana ray is prone to fits of aggression, moreso than usual.', -1, 0),
(402672, 15, 5, 'Bloodtooth Mana Ray', 402672, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402672, 6, 1, 'The shattering of Argus drove this breed of mana ray to bloodthirst. It now subsists on the corrupted blood of any creatures it can sink its many teeth into.', -1, 0),
(402673, 15, 5, 'Albino Mana Ray', 402673, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402673, 6, 1, 'The shattering of Argus caused the mana rays to mutate and adapt to their surroundings. Some of them abandoned their pigments in favor of strengthening their senses.', -1, 0),
(402674, 15, 5, 'Luminous Mana Ray', 402674, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402674, 6, 1, 'Mana rays can emit a bright glow to lure in prey.', -1, 0),
(402675, 15, 5, 'Twilight Courser', 402675, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402675, 6, 1, 'To evade predators, this courser dims its horn while hiding and flashes with dazzling radiance when provoked.', -1, 0),
(402676, 15, 5, 'Golden Sunrunner', 402676, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402676, 6, 1, 'This free spirit enjoys long trots on the beach and frolicking through varicolored floral fields.', -1, 0),
(402677, 15, 5, 'Turquoise Courser', 402677, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402677, 6, 1, 'Named for its uniquely colored eyes that seem to pierce your soul, the turquoise courser shows more intelligence than her dreamrunner cousins and is known to be an excellent judge of character.', -1, 0),
(402678, 15, 5, 'Gloomdark Nightmare', 402678, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402678, 6, 1, 'Touched by the Emerald Nightmare, this creature\'s presence in one\'s dreams is an omen of misfortune. To see one while awake portends absolute catastrophe.', -1, 0),
(402679, 15, 5, 'Bonesteed of Triumph', 402679, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402679, 6, 1, 'A good warhorse is loyal to its bones. Having shed its mortal coil, this steed is an omen of bold conquest.', -1, 0),
(402681, 15, 5, 'Bonesteed of Bloodshed', 402681, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402681, 6, 1, 'A good warhorse is loyal to its bones. Having shed its mortal coil, this steed is an omen of eternal strife.', -1, 0),
(402682, 15, 5, 'Bonesteed of Plague', 402682, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402682, 6, 1, 'A good warhorse is loyal to its bones. Having shed its mortal coil, this steed is an omen of sickness and suffering.', -1, 0),
(402683, 15, 5, 'Bonesteed of Oblivion', 402683, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402683, 6, 1, 'A good warhorse is loyal to its bones. Having shed its mortal coil, this steed is an omen of scarcity and death.', -1, 0),
(402686, 15, 5, 'Longhorned Sable Talbuk', 402686, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402686, 6, 1, 'The talbuks of Argus have grown long, coarse fur of brilliant colors that reflects the hues of their broken planet.', -1, 0),
(402688, 15, 5, 'Garnet Ruinstrider', 402688, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402688, 6, 1, 'Outfitted with sturdy barding, Argussian ruinstriders fearlessly carry their riders across the broken wastes of Argus and beyond.', -1, 0),
(402689, 15, 5, 'Longhorned Bleakhoof Talbuk', 402689, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402689, 6, 1, 'Scarred by the chaos wrought by decades of conflict, this fel-infused steed is a perfect match for an intrepid adventurer.', -1, 0),
(402690, 15, 5, 'Longhorned Argussian Talbuk', 402690, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402690, 6, 1, 'Few talbuks managed to remain unscathed despite the Legion\'s exploitation of their homeworld. Their tenacity is befitting of a noble steed.', -1, 0),
(402691, 15, 5, 'Longhorned Beryl Talbuk', 402691, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402691, 6, 1, 'This wild talbuk found among the ruins of Argus has survived and persevered through decades of strife.', -1, 0),
(402693, 15, 5, 'Amani Sunfeather', 402693, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402693, 6, 1, 'Born of Abundance and the forest\'s renewal, these eagles gleam in the setting sun, a living sign of the Amani\'s rekindled strength.', -1, 0),
(402694, 15, 5, 'Amani Windcaller', 402694, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402694, 6, 1, 'Swift as the storm and sharp as lightning, these sacred eagles bear the mark of Akil\'zon, carrying their riders on the winds of her blessing.', -1, 0),
(402696, 15, 5, 'Highlands Gobbler', 402696, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402696, 6, 1, 'Fierce and very large turkeys are now occasionally seen roaming the deep forests of Tirisfal after the blighting during the Fourth War.', -1, 0),
(402697, 15, 5, 'Quirky Turkey', 402697, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402697, 6, 1, 'This creature might not be majestic but it certainly will turn heads!', -1, 0),
(402698, 15, 5, 'Aubergine Warturkey', 402698, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402698, 6, 1, 'Its crimes can not be pardoned.', -1, 0),
(402699, 15, 5, 'Prized Turkey', 402699, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402699, 6, 1, 'This extra-large turkey not only took first place due to its pristine feathers, but also for its larger-than-average size.', -1, 0),
(402700, 15, 5, 'Frostfall Groveglider', 402700, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402700, 6, 1, 'These high-flying denizens of Azeroth\'s tallest trees have developed a thick, silky coat to adapt to even the coldest climates.', -1, 0),
(402701, 15, 5, 'Cindertuft Groveglider', 402701, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402701, 6, 1, 'Native to Hyjal, these mischievous tree-dwellers underwent a startling transformation when the Firelands made its appearance in the region.', -1, 0),
(402702, 15, 5, 'Gloombough Groveglider', 402702, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402702, 6, 1, 'The Gloombough not only have uniquely dark coloring, but are entirely nocturnal, making them one of the rarest tree-dwellers to spot in person.', -1, 0),
(402703, 15, 5, 'Blossombranch Groveglider', 402703, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402703, 6, 1, 'These enchanting grovegliders are known for their coloring, reminiscent of some of Pandaria\'s treasured blossoming trees.', -1, 0),
(402705, 15, 5, 'Chestnut Courser', 402705, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402705, 6, 1, 'Coursers make for excellent steeds. Just don\'t try to dismount from their front.', -1, 0),
(402706, 15, 5, 'Brimstone Courser', 402706, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402706, 6, 1, 'The flames of a courser\'s hooves express their affinity for a particular school of magic.', -1, 0),
(402707, 15, 5, 'Brilliant Petalwing', 402707, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402707, 6, 1, 'This beast glows with a radiance no void could suppress.', -1, 0),
(402708, 15, 5, 'Vibrant Petalwing', 402708, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402708, 6, 1, 'Filling the skies of Harandar with a striking pink hue, the Vibrant Petalwing attained its noteworthy pigment through the nectar of various flora it consumes.', -1, 0),
(402710, 15, 5, 'Cerulean Sporeglider', 402710, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402710, 6, 1, 'This sporeglider likes to gently nuzzle its riders.', -1, 0),
(402713, 15, 5, 'Ruddy Sporeglider', 402713, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402713, 6, 1, 'This sporeglider derived its striking hue from the unique fungus growing around Teldrassil\'s roots.', -1, 0),
(402717, 15, 5, 'Mechanical Prototype Panther MK-0', 402717, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402717, 6, 1, 'When Gadgetzan citizens pried open Gazlowe palace\'s underground lab, caged beasts\' roars were suffocating. Undermine tech fused combat modules onto these panthers, granting superhuman strength and speed.', -1, 0),
(402718, 15, 5, 'Steel Prototype Panther MK-0', 402718, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402718, 6, 1, 'The first Steel Horde soldiers crossing the Dark Portal captured a ferocious nightsaber. Blackrock artisans armed it with magma armor, transforming it into a combat weapon.', -1, 0),
(402719, 15, 5, 'Starspark Netherdrake', 402719, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402719, 6, 1, 'After flying you to the ends of Outland and beyond, the netherwing drake was eventually drawn to the blue skies of Azeroth as well.', -1, 0),
(402720, 15, 5, 'Felscorned Vilebrood Vanquisher', 402720, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402720, 6, 1, 'This flying amalgamation of the forces of death and fel pierces the skies with a bone-chilling screech.', -1, 0),
(402721, 15, 5, 'Slayer\'s Felscorned Shrieker', 402721, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402721, 6, 1, 'Torn from the heavens by only the most cunning of Demon Hunters.', -1, 0),
(402723, 15, 5, 'Felscorned Wolfhawk', 402723, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402723, 6, 1, 'Scarred by the war across the Broken Isles, this Wolfhawk deserves a good home.', -1, 0),
(402724, 15, 5, 'Archmage\'s Felscorned Disc', 402724, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402724, 6, 1, 'Some mages say fel magics are "volatile" or "corruptive" or "forbidden". Some mages are wrong.', -1, 0),
(402725, 15, 5, 'Felscorned Grandmaster\'s Companion', 402725, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402725, 6, 1, 'A twisted visage of a beloved companion.', -1, 0),
(402726, 15, 5, 'Felscorned Highlord\'s Charger', 402726, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402726, 6, 1, 'This horse has been irreversibly scarred by the Legion\'s corrupt magics.', -1, 0),
(402727, 15, 5, 'High Priest\'s Felscorned Seeker', 402727, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402727, 6, 1, 'This fel-infused feathered friend flaps its wings at a frenetic pace to remain far above the frenzy below.', -1, 0),
(402728, 15, 5, 'Shadowblade\'s Felscorned Omen', 402728, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402728, 6, 1, 'Your enemies will know fear before their end.', -1, 0),
(402729, 15, 5, 'Farseer\'s Felscorned Tempest', 402729, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402729, 6, 1, 'Fel flavored fury.', -1, 0),
(402730, 15, 5, 'Felscorned Netherlord\'s Dreadsteed', 402730, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402730, 6, 1, 'Simply oozing with potential.', -1, 0),
(402731, 15, 5, 'Felscorned War Wyrm', 402731, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402731, 6, 1, 'The heavens tremble in anticipation of your arrival.', -1, 0),
(402732, 15, 5, 'Cobalt Phase-Hunter', 402732, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402732, 6, 1, 'Due to the otherworldly energies that irradiated Draenor, these creatures can shift through space at will. As such, they are rarely seen... until it is too late.', -1, 0),
(402733, 15, 5, 'Calamitous Carrion', 402733, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402733, 6, 1, 'Bearing Zul\'Aman\'s fiercest riders, its shadowed wings strike down any who dare resist.', -1, 0),
(402734, 15, 5, 'Convalescent Carrion', 402734, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402734, 6, 1, 'Circling above the dying and the doomed, its wings herald plague, ruin, and the certainty that nothing left in its shadow will rise again.', -1, 0),
(402742, 15, 5, 'Thunderhoof Celestial', 402742, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402742, 6, 1, 'After the Thunder King\'s fall, his lingering thunder merged with the spirit of a white dragon. It strides on azure lightning, clouds swirling in its wake-where tyranny once reigned, now guardian light remains.', -1, 0),
(402743, 15, 5, 'Stormgilded Celestial', 402743, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402743, 6, 1, 'Gilded in thunder, chosen by destiny. Golden lightning wraps its hooves, piercing the sky like tearing through night. Legends tie it closely to Emperor Shaohao.', -1, 0),
(402747, 15, 5, 'Untainted Grove Crawler', 402747, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402747, 6, 1, 'Somehow this grove crawler remains untouched by the horrors that overran Fungara Village.', -1, 0),
(402749, 15, 5, 'Echo of Aln\'sharan', 402749, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402749, 6, 1, 'Heed well the song of the Goddess.', -1, 0),
(402751, 15, 5, 'Augmented Stormray', 402751, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402751, 6, 1, 'Captured from K\'aresh and mutated by Charonus, this stormray escaped from Voidscar Arena and has wandered the Voidstorm.', -1, 0),
(402753, 15, 5, 'Fiery Dragonhawk', 402753, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402753, 6, 1, 'A dragonhawk whose wings shine as brightly as the leaves of its Eversong home.', -1, 0),
(402754, 15, 5, 'Peridot Dragonhawk', 402754, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402754, 6, 1, 'Peridot dragonhawks are only awarded to those who have performed great deeds in service of Silvermoon.', -1, 0),
(402755, 15, 5, 'Umbral Dragonhawk', 402755, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402755, 6, 1, 'Cloaked in blackened tones, this Dragonhawk glides with calm precision, its somber coloring lending it an air of quiet distinction.', -1, 0),
(402756, 15, 5, 'Crimson Dragonhawk', 402756, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402756, 6, 1, 'A strikingly colored Dragonhawk admired across Quel\'Thalas, its vivid red wings cutting bright arcs through the skies as it glides with smooth, effortless grace.', -1, 0),
(402758, 15, 5, 'Cobalt Dragonhawk', 402758, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402758, 6, 1, 'A rare breed of Dragonhawk that soars the Thalassian skies on azure wings after having escaped from the Sunwing Rookery.', -1, 0),
(402760, 15, 5, 'Amani Sharptalon', 402760, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402760, 6, 1, 'A rare variety of the Amani eagle, Sharptalons strike with terrifying precision and fly with unparalleled grace.', -1, 0),
(402761, 15, 5, 'Crimson Silvermoon Hawkstrider', 402761, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402761, 6, 1, 'The pride of the Silvermoon Court, these hawkstriders are prized for their vibrant red plumage and purebred elegance.', -1, 0),
(402762, 15, 5, 'Cerulean Hawkstrider', 402762, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402762, 6, 1, 'A brilliant-plumed hawkstrider that escaped from the Silvermoon stables, who knows where in Eversong it may be hiding?', -1, 0),
(402764, 15, 5, 'Duskbrute Harrower', 402764, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402764, 6, 1, 'These harrowers are attracted to the constant battle cries and bloodshed across Slayer\'s Rise.', -1, 0),
(402767, 15, 5, 'Contained Stormarion Defender', 402767, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402767, 6, 1, 'While often aggressive, some Harrowers can be tamed and taught to aid in defensive military techniques. This Harrower looks over the Stormarion Core to ensure none can breach it.', -1, 0),
(402769, 15, 5, 'Preyseeker\'s Hubris', 402769, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402769, 6, 1, 'Larger mana wyrms are sometimes used as mounts by Blood Elves, but are more frequently kept as status symbols.', -1, 0),
(402770, 15, 5, 'Preyseeker\'s Wrath', 402770, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402770, 6, 1, 'Mana wyrms that are large and strong enough to support full barding and rider are quite rare and highly prized.', -1, 0),
(402771, 15, 5, 'Preyseeker\'s Nightmare', 402771, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402771, 6, 1, 'Golden mana wyrms are an uncommon mutation. Some of Astalor\'s side experiments have included efforts to increase their population..', -1, 0),
(402772, 15, 5, 'Blessed Amani Burrower', 402772, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402772, 6, 1, 'A creature blessed by the wilds, it moves with the steadfast spirit and gentle strength the Amani hold sacred.', -1, 0),
(402773, 15, 5, 'Giganto Manis', 402773, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402773, 6, 1, 'Whispers tell of the Giganto Manis, a titanic creature said to dwell within Azeroth\'s very veins.', -1, 0),
(402775, 15, 5, 'Witherbark Pango', 402775, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402775, 6, 1, 'This rather rambunctious Pango escaped from the Witherbark Tribe after having its armor affixed. Finders keepers!', -1, 0),
(402776, 15, 5, 'Amani Blessed Bear', 402776, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402776, 6, 1, 'Once symbols of conquest, these war-bears now stride again, reborn through Nalorakk\'s blessing and the renewed spirit of the Amani.', -1, 0),
(402778, 15, 5, 'Ancestral War Bear', 402778, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402778, 6, 1, 'Its tread resounds with the memory of ancient warriors, a living symbol of the unwavering ferocity the Amani revere.', -1, 0),
(402779, 15, 5, 'Witherbark Warbear Mother', 402779, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402779, 6, 1, 'This warbear mother was captured by the Twilight\'s Blade while protecting her cub. Her continued separation from her cub is only angering her more. Anyone who manages to reunite her with her cub will have her eternal loyalty.', -1, 0),
(402781, 15, 5, 'Amani Hex Bear', 402781, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402781, 6, 1, 'Tricked into fighting along the Hex, this fierce creature now fights for the Amani tribe, hoping to find its way back into the good graces of Nalorakk.', -1, 0),
(402785, 15, 5, 'Relinquished Scarlet Charger', 402785, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402785, 6, 1, 'No longer a tool of the Scarlet Crusade, this charger now guides recruits down the path of the Light with renewed purpose.', -1, 0),
(402786, 15, 5, 'Hexed Vilefeather Eagle', 402786, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402786, 6, 1, 'Once a proud sky-hunter, she now soars on withered wings, her spirit twisted by lingering necromantic curses that seep through every rotting plume and ghostlit eye.', -1, 0),
(402789, 15, 5, 'Ravenous Shredclaw', 402789, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402789, 6, 1, 'Fast and dependable, Shredclaws were one of the first creatures tamed in the Voidstorm. Their owners learned quickly not to leave them alone with their pets.', -1, 0),
(402790, 15, 5, 'Insatiable Shredclaw', 402790, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402790, 6, 1, 'The shredclaw has fully embraced the way of the Void: never satisfied, constantly seeking out new strength to dominate and new prey to devour.', -1, 0),
(402791, 15, 5, 'Prowling Shredclaw', 402791, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402791, 6, 1, 'According to ren\'dorei scouts, shredclaws are often seen hunting in packs.', -1, 0),
(402792, 15, 5, 'Frenzied Shredclaw', 402792, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402792, 6, 1, 'Once a pack member dies, these shredclaws enter a frenzy of rage that not even a hulking ultradon can stop.', -1, 0),
(402793, 15, 5, 'Vicious Snaplizard', 402793, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402793, 6, 1, 'These creatures are found sneaking through the battlefield and climbing over obstactles, ready to cause trouble for the Alliance.', -1, 0),
(402794, 15, 5, 'Vicious Snaplizard', 402794, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402794, 6, 1, 'These creatures are found sneaking through the battlefield and climbing over obstactles, ready to cause trouble for the Horde.', -1, 0),
(402795, 15, 5, 'Bronze Wilderling', 402795, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402795, 6, 1, 'The regal wilderlings twist through the sky, free as the unbound magic that sustains their flight.', -1, 0),
(402796, 15, 5, 'Bronze Aquilon', 402796, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402796, 6, 1, 'The reliable steeds of Bastion are designed to mirror the proud and noble warriors of the Ascended.', -1, 0),
(402797, 15, 5, 'Bronze Corpsefly', 402797, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402797, 6, 1, 'It takes a great deal of effort to decorate a corpsefly, but some would say the efforts are worth it.', -1, 0),
(402798, 15, 5, 'Bronze Gravewing', 402798, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402798, 6, 1, 'While dark and ominous is the preferred aesthetic of those who reside in Revendreth, there are some who still favor gleaming luster.', -1, 0),
(402801, 15, 5, 'Galactic Gladiator\'s Goredrake', 402801, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402801, 6, 1, 'Originating from the void, fully armored and ready for combat.', -1, 0),
(402802, 15, 5, 'Geargrinder Mk. 11', 402802, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402802, 6, 1, 'Undergoes a new iteration each time it explodes!', -1, 0),
(402803, 15, 5, 'Skypaw Glimmerfur', 402803, 4, 0, 0, 0, 20, 762, 75, 0, 55884, -1, 402803, 6, 1, 'A Glimmerfur\'s coat takes on properties of its environment much like a camouflage. Patterns of bright blue skies and majestic white clouds have earned this glimmerfur the nickname "Skypaw."', -1, 0),
